window.TWG_L1C={"level":1,"exam":{"questions":30,"minutes":45,"pass":70,"written":false,"tasting":false,"trueFalse":true},"ch":{"p1":{"it":"L'uva, la vite e il clima","fr":"Le raisin, la vigne et le climat","en":"Grapes, vines and climate"},"p2":{"it":"Come si fa il vino","fr":"Comment on fait le vin","en":"How wine is made"},"w1":{"it":"Tipi e stili di vino","fr":"Types et styles de vins","en":"Types and styles of wine"},"w2":{"it":"I quattro bianchi principali","fr":"Les quatre grands blancs","en":"The four key white grapes"},"w3":{"it":"I quattro rossi principali","fr":"Les quatre grands rouges","en":"The four key black grapes"},"w4":{"it":"Vini famosi dai vitigni principali","fr":"Vins célèbres des grands cépages","en":"Famous wines from the key grapes"},"w5":{"it":"Altri vini da conoscere","fr":"Autres vins à connaître","en":"Other wines to know"},"t1":{"it":"Conservare e servire il vino","fr":"Conserver et servir le vin","en":"Storing and serving wine"},"t2":{"it":"Cibo e vino","fr":"Mets et vins","en":"Food and wine"},"t3":{"it":"Degustare: i primi passi","fr":"Déguster : premiers pas","en":"Tasting: first steps"}},"groups":[{"k":"p","w":6,"n":{"it":"Dalla vigna al vino","fr":"De la vigne au vin","en":"From vine to wine"},"c":["p1","p2"]},{"k":"w","w":18,"n":{"it":"Tipi, stili e vitigni","fr":"Types, styles et cépages","en":"Types, styles and grapes"},"c":["w1","w2","w3","w4","w5"]},{"k":"t","w":6,"n":{"it":"Conservare, servire, abbinare","fr":"Conserver, servir, accorder","en":"Store, serve, pair"},"c":["t1","t2","t3"]}],"bank":[{"id":"l1713c3a1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale definizione descrive meglio il vino?","Quelle définition décrit le mieux le vin ?","Which definition best describes wine?"],"o":[["Succo d'uva fermentato","Du jus de raisin fermenté","Fermented grape juice"],["Succo d'uva distillato","Du jus de raisin distillé","Distilled grape juice"],["Succo d'uva concentrato","Du jus de raisin concentré","Concentrated grape juice"],["Succo d'uva pastorizzato","Du jus de raisin pasteurisé","Pasteurised grape juice"]],"e":["Il vino si ottiene facendo fermentare il succo dolce dell'uva.","Le vin s'obtient en faisant fermenter le jus sucré du raisin.","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes."],"d":["Per fare il vino si schiaccia l'uva per liberarne il succo dolce. Poi la fermentazione alcolica, grazie ai lieviti, trasforma lo zucchero di quel succo in alcol. Senza fermentazione resterebbe semplice succo d'uva; la distillazione o la concentrazione non fanno parte della definizione di base del vino.","Pour faire du vin, on écrase le raisin afin de libérer son jus sucré. Ensuite, la fermentation alcoolique, grâce aux levures, transforme le sucre de ce jus en alcool. Sans fermentation, il ne resterait qu'un jus de raisin ; la distillation ou la concentration ne font pas partie de la définition de base du vin.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine."]},{"id":"l122a0219","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In quale parte dell'uva nera si trovano i tannini?","Dans quelle partie du raisin noir trouve-t-on les tanins ?","Which part of a black grape contains tannins?"],"o":[["Nella buccia","Dans la peau","The skin"],["Nella polpa","Dans la pulpe","The pulp"],["Nel succo","Dans le jus","The juice"],["Nel fiore","Dans la fleur","The flower"]],"e":["La buccia delle uve nere contiene sia il colore sia i tannini.","La peau des raisins noirs contient à la fois la couleur et les tanins.","Black grape skins hold both the colour and the tannins."],"d":["La buccia è la parte che distingue davvero le uve nere da quelle bianche: è intensamente colorata e contiene tannini, che lasciano in bocca una sensazione di secchezza. La polpa invece contiene il succo, fatto di acqua, zucchero e acido, ed è dello stesso colore in tutte le uve.","La peau est ce qui distingue vraiment les raisins noirs des blancs : elle est très colorée et contient des tanins, qui donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche. La pulpe, elle, contient le jus, fait d'eau, de sucre et d'acide, et elle a la même couleur dans tous les raisins.","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes."]},{"id":"l168e9f05","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Da che cosa è composto principalmente il succo della polpa?","De quoi est principalement composé le jus de la pulpe ?","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?"],"o":[["Acqua, zucchero e acido","Eau, sucre et acide","Water, sugar and acid"],["Acqua, tannini e colore","Eau, tanins et couleur","Water, tannin and colour"],["Alcol, zucchero e lievito","Alcool, sucre et levures","Alcohol, sugar and yeast"],["Acqua, alcol e anidride carbonica","Eau, alcool et gaz carbonique","Water, alcohol and carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Il succo d'uva è soprattutto acqua, zucchero e acido.","Le jus de raisin est surtout composé d'eau, de sucre et d'acide.","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid."],"d":["La polpa è la parte morbida dell'acino e contiene il succo, formato in gran parte da acqua, zucchero e acido. Tannini e colore stanno invece nella buccia. Alcol e anidride carbonica compaiono solo più tardi, quando i lieviti fermentano lo zucchero del succo.","La pulpe est la partie tendre du grain et contient le jus, composé en grande partie d'eau, de sucre et d'acide. Les tanins et la couleur se trouvent dans la peau. L'alcool et le gaz carbonique n'apparaissent que plus tard, quand les levures font fermenter le sucre du jus.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice."]},{"id":"l11f3fcad","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che sensazione lasciano in bocca i tannini?","Quelle sensation les tanins laissent-ils en bouche ?","What do tannins do to your mouth?"],"o":[["La fanno sentire secca","Ils l'assèchent","Make it feel dry"],["La fanno salivare","Ils la font saliver","Make it water"],["La fanno sentire calda","Ils la réchauffent","Make it feel hot"],["La fanno sentire dolce","Ils l'adoucissent","Make it feel sweet"]],"e":["I tannini della buccia danno una sensazione di secchezza in bocca.","Les tanins de la peau donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche.","Tannins from the skins leave the mouth feeling dry."],"d":["I tannini provengono dalla buccia delle uve nere e si percepiscono più come una sensazione che come un sapore: asciugano la bocca. Non vanno confusi con l'acidità, che invece fa salivare, né con l'alcol, che dà una sensazione di calore.","Les tanins viennent de la peau des raisins noirs et se perçoivent davantage comme une sensation que comme un goût : ils assèchent la bouche. Il ne faut pas les confondre avec l'acidité, qui fait saliver, ni avec l'alcool, qui donne une sensation de chaleur.","Tannins come from black grape skins and are felt more than tasted: they dry out the mouth. When tasting, they should not be confused with acidity, which makes your mouth water instead, or with alcohol, which gives a warming sensation."]},{"id":"l1bbb6c87","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che colore ha la polpa di un'uva nera?","Quelle est la couleur de la pulpe d'un raisin noir ?","What colour is the pulp of a black grape?"],"o":[["Lo stesso di quella di un'uva bianca","La même que celle d'un raisin blanc","The same as in a white grape"],["Rosso intenso, come la buccia","Rouge intense, comme la peau","Deep red, like the skin"],["Viola, ma solo a piena maturità","Violette, mais seulement à maturité","Purple, but only when fully ripe"],["Rosa, più chiara della buccia","Rose, plus claire que la peau","Pink, paler than the skin"]],"e":["La polpa ha lo stesso colore in tutte le uve; il colore sta nella buccia.","La pulpe a la même couleur dans tous les raisins ; la couleur est dans la peau.","Pulp is the same colour in all grapes; the colour is in the skin."],"d":["All'interno uve bianche e nere si somigliano molto: la polpa ha lo stesso colore, qualunque sia il colore della buccia. È proprio per questo che il colore di un vino rosso viene dalle bucce, e che da uve nere si può persino ottenere un vino bianco separando subito il succo dalle bucce.","À l'intérieur, raisins blancs et noirs se ressemblent beaucoup : la pulpe a la même couleur, quelle que soit celle de la peau. C'est pour cela que la couleur d'un vin rouge vient des peaux, et qu'on peut même faire un vin blanc avec des raisins noirs en séparant tout de suite le jus des peaux.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away."]},{"id":"l1bbb5fa6","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In quale stagione fiorisce la vite?","À quelle saison la vigne fleurit-elle ?","In which season does the grape vine flower?"],"o":[["In primavera","Au printemps","Spring"],["In estate","En été","Summer"],["In autunno","En automne","Autumn"],["In inverno","En hiver","Winter"]],"e":["La vite fiorisce in primavera; l'uva matura poi in estate.","La vigne fleurit au printemps ; le raisin mûrit ensuite en été.","Vines flower in spring; the grapes then ripen in summer."],"d":["Il ciclo annuale della vite segue le stagioni. In primavera compaiono i grappoli di fiori, ciascuno dei quali diventerà un acino. In estate l'uva matura e verso la fine dell'estate si vendemmia. In inverno, invece, la vite riposa, e ha bisogno di un freddo sufficiente per farlo.","Le cycle annuel de la vigne suit les saisons. Au printemps apparaissent les grappes de fleurs, dont chacune deviendra un grain. En été, le raisin mûrit, et vers la fin de l'été on vendange. En hiver, en revanche, la vigne se repose, et elle a besoin d'un froid suffisant pour cela.","The vine's yearly cycle follows the seasons. In spring the clusters of flowers appear, and each flower will become a grape. During summer the grapes ripen, and they are picked towards the end of summer. In winter the vine rests, and it needs enough cold to do so."]},{"id":"l13597bf0","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa diventa ogni fiore della vite?","Que devient chaque fleur de la vigne ?","What does each individual vine flower become?"],"o":[["Un acino d'uva","Un grain de raisin","One grape"],["Un nuovo germoglio","Une nouvelle pousse","A new shoot"],["Un'intera foglia","Une feuille entière","A whole leaf"],["Un grappolo intero","Une grappe entière","A whole bunch"]],"e":["Dopo la fioritura ogni singolo fiore si trasforma in un piccolo acino.","Après la floraison, chaque fleur se transforme en un petit grain.","After flowering, each single flower turns into a small grape."],"d":["I fiori della vite si presentano a grappoli formati da tanti fiori piccolissimi. Dopo la fioritura ognuno di essi diventa un acino: il grappolo di fiori diventa quindi un grappolo d'uva. All'inizio questi acini sono piccoli, duri e verdi, e solo durante l'estate cresceranno e matureranno.","Les fleurs de vigne forment des grappes composées de nombreuses fleurs minuscules. Après la floraison, chacune devient un grain : la grappe de fleurs devient donc une grappe de raisin. Au début, ces grains sont petits, durs et verts ; ils ne grossiront et ne mûriront qu'au cours de l'été.","Vine flowers come in clusters made up of many tiny flowers. After flowering, each one becomes a grape, so the cluster of flowers turns into a bunch of grapes. At first these grapes are small, hard and green; they only grow and ripen as the summer goes on."]},{"id":"l13008e68","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Come sono gli acini subito dopo la fioritura?","Comment sont les grains juste après la floraison ?","What are grapes like just after flowering?"],"o":[["Piccoli, duri e verdi","Petits, durs et verts","Small, hard and green"],["Piccoli, morbidi e dorati","Petits, mous et dorés","Small, soft and golden"],["Grossi, duri e viola","Gros, durs et violets","Large, hard and purple"],["Grossi, morbidi e dolci","Gros, mous et sucrés","Large, soft and sweet"]],"e":["Tutti gli acini giovani sono piccoli, duri e verdi, bianchi o neri che siano.","Tous les jeunes grains sont petits, durs et verts, blancs ou noirs.","All young grapes are small, hard and green, white or black."],"d":["Appena formati, gli acini non sono ancora pronti: sono piccoli, duri e verdi, e in questa fase uve bianche e nere non si distinguono. Solo con la maturazione estiva si gonfiano d'acqua, diventano più dolci e cambiano colore, verso il dorato per le bianche e verso il viola per le nere.","Juste formés, les grains ne sont pas encore prêts : ils sont petits, durs et verts, et à ce stade on ne distingue pas les raisins blancs des noirs. Ce n'est qu'avec la maturation estivale qu'ils gonflent d'eau, deviennent plus sucrés et changent de couleur, vers le doré pour les blancs et vers le violet pour les noirs.","Newly formed grapes are not ready yet: they are small, hard and green, and at this stage white and black grapes look the same. Only during summer ripening do they swell with water, become sweeter and change colour, towards golden for white grapes and purple for black ones."]},{"id":"l12811d78","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Durante la maturazione, che cosa succede ai livelli di zucchero e di acido nell'uva?","Pendant la maturation, que deviennent les niveaux de sucre et d'acide du raisin ?","As grapes ripen, what happens to their sugar and acid levels?"],"o":[["Lo zucchero sale e l'acido scende","Le sucre augmente et l'acide diminue","Sugar rises and acid falls"],["Lo zucchero scende e l'acido sale","Le sucre diminue et l'acide augmente","Sugar falls and acid rises"],["Salgono entrambi allo stesso ritmo","Les deux augmentent au même rythme","Both rise at the same rate"],["Restano entrambi invariati","Les deux restent stables","Both stay the same"]],"e":["Maturando l'uva diventa più dolce e meno acida.","En mûrissant, le raisin devient plus sucré et moins acide.","Ripening makes grapes sweeter and less acidic."],"d":["Mentre l'uva matura in estate avvengono diversi cambiamenti: gli acini si gonfiano d'acqua, lo zucchero aumenta, l'acido diminuisce e i sapori diventano più maturi. È questo equilibrio tra zucchero e acido che, più tardi, influenzerà l'alcol e la freschezza del vino.","Pendant que le raisin mûrit en été, plusieurs changements se produisent : les grains gonflent d'eau, le sucre augmente, l'acide diminue et les saveurs deviennent plus mûres. C'est cet équilibre entre sucre et acide qui influencera plus tard l'alcool et la fraîcheur du vin.","While grapes ripen over the summer, several things change: they swell with water, sugar goes up, acid goes down and the flavours become riper. This balance between sugar and acid will later influence the alcohol and freshness of the wine."]},{"id":"l1bb25208","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Di che colore diventano le uve bianche quando maturano?","Quelle couleur prennent les raisins blancs en mûrissant ?","What colour do white grapes turn as they ripen?"],"o":[["Dal verde al dorato","Du vert au doré","From green to golden"],["Dal verde al viola","Du vert au violet","From green to purple"],["Dal giallo al verde","Du jaune au vert","From yellow to green"],["Dal dorato al rosa","Du doré au rose","From golden to pink"]],"e":["Le uve bianche passano dal verde al dorato; le nere dal verde al viola.","Les raisins blancs passent du vert au doré ; les noirs du vert au violet.","White grapes go from green to golden; black ones from green to purple."],"d":["All'inizio tutti gli acini sono verdi. Con la maturazione la buccia cambia colore: nelle uve bianche diventa dorata, nelle uve nere diventa viola. Il cambiamento di colore accompagna gli altri segni della maturazione, cioè più acqua, più zucchero, meno acido e sapori più maturi.","Au départ, tous les grains sont verts. Avec la maturation, la peau change de couleur : elle devient dorée chez les raisins blancs et violette chez les raisins noirs. Ce changement accompagne les autres signes de maturation : plus d'eau, plus de sucre, moins d'acide et des saveurs plus mûres.","At first all grapes are green. As they ripen, the skin changes colour: it becomes golden in white grapes and purple in black grapes. This colour change goes hand in hand with the other signs of ripening, namely more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours."]},{"id":"l1c26259b","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi cambiamenti NON avviene quando l'uva matura?","Lequel de ces changements ne se produit PAS quand le raisin mûrit ?","Which of these does NOT happen as grapes ripen?"],"o":[["L'acidità aumenta","L'acidité augmente","Acidity increases"],["Gli acini si gonfiano d'acqua","Les grains gonflent d'eau","Grapes swell with water"],["Lo zucchero aumenta","Le sucre augmente","Sugar increases"],["I sapori diventano più maturi","Les saveurs deviennent plus mûres","Flavours become riper"]],"e":["Con la maturazione l'acidità scende, non sale.","En mûrissant, l'acidité baisse, elle n'augmente pas.","During ripening acidity falls, it does not rise."],"d":["La maturazione porta più acqua negli acini, più zucchero e sapori più maturi, ma l'acido segue la direzione opposta e diminuisce. Per questo un'uva acerba è aspra, mentre un'uva matura è dolce e meno acida. Ricordare questa tendenza aiuta anche a capire l'effetto del clima.","La maturation apporte plus d'eau dans les grains, plus de sucre et des saveurs plus mûres, mais l'acide suit le chemin inverse et diminue. C'est pourquoi un raisin vert est acide, tandis qu'un raisin mûr est sucré et moins acide. Retenir cette tendance aide aussi à comprendre l'effet du climat.","Ripening brings more water into the grapes, more sugar and riper flavours, but acid moves the other way and drops. That is why an unripe grape tastes sour, while a ripe one is sweet and less acidic. Remembering this trend also helps you understand the effect of climate."]},{"id":"l15a7a1c1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quando si vendemmia di solito, secondo il ciclo della vite?","Quand vendange-t-on habituellement, selon le cycle de la vigne ?","In the vine's yearly cycle, when are the grapes usually picked?"],"o":[["Verso la fine dell'estate","Vers la fin de l'été","In late summer"],["All'inizio della primavera","Au début du printemps","In early spring"],["In pieno inverno","En plein hiver","In midwinter"],["Subito dopo la fioritura","Juste après la floraison","Just after flowering"]],"e":["L'uva matura durante l'estate e si raccoglie verso la fine dell'estate.","Le raisin mûrit pendant l'été et se récolte vers la fin de l'été.","Grapes ripen through summer and are picked in late summer."],"d":["La vite fiorisce in primavera, i fiori diventano acini e questi maturano durante l'estate. Quando sono abbastanza maturi, verso la fine dell'estate, si raccolgono. Subito dopo la fioritura gli acini sono ancora piccoli, duri e verdi, quindi troppo acerbi per fare vino.","La vigne fleurit au printemps, les fleurs deviennent des grains, et ceux-ci mûrissent pendant l'été. Lorsqu'ils sont assez mûrs, vers la fin de l'été, on les récolte. Juste après la floraison, les grains sont encore petits, durs et verts, donc beaucoup trop peu mûrs pour faire du vin.","The vine flowers in spring, the flowers become grapes and these ripen during the summer. Once they are ripe enough, towards the end of summer, they are picked. Just after flowering the grapes are still small, hard and green, far too unripe to make wine."]},{"id":"l1b4557c0","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché la vite cresce meglio dove l'inverno è freddo?","Pourquoi la vigne pousse-t-elle mieux là où l'hiver est froid ?","Why do vines grow best where winters are cold?"],"o":[["Perché il freddo le permette di riposare","Parce que le froid lui permet de se reposer","The cold lets the vine rest"],["Perché il freddo aumenta lo zucchero","Parce que le froid augmente le sucre","The cold raises sugar levels"],["Perché il freddo fa fiorire la vite","Parce que le froid fait fleurir la vigne","The cold makes the vine flower"],["Perché il freddo colora le bucce","Parce que le froid colore les peaux","The cold colours the skins"]],"e":["Un inverno abbastanza freddo dà alla vite un periodo di riposo.","Un hiver assez froid offre à la vigne une période de repos.","A cold enough winter gives the vine a period of rest."],"d":["Oltre alla giusta quantità di sole e calore durante la stagione di crescita, la vite ha bisogno di un inverno abbastanza freddo da poter riposare. Per questo la maggior parte dei vigneti si trova in fasce di latitudine precise, né troppo fredde né troppo calde.","En plus de la bonne dose de soleil et de chaleur pendant la saison de croissance, la vigne a besoin d'un hiver assez froid pour pouvoir se reposer. C'est pourquoi la plupart des vignobles se trouvent dans des bandes de latitude précises, ni trop froides ni trop chaudes.","Besides the right amount of sunlight and heat during the growing season, a vine needs a winter cold enough to let it rest. This is why most vineyards are found in particular bands of latitude, neither too cold nor too hot."]},{"id":"l10de113c","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi Paesi è un esempio di clima fresco per la vite?","Lequel de ces pays est un exemple de climat frais pour la vigne ?","Which of these is an example of a cool climate wine region?"],"o":[["La Germania","L'Allemagne","Germany"],["Alcune zone dell'Australia","Certaines zones d'Australie","Parts of Australia"],["Alcune zone della California","Certaines zones de Californie","Parts of California"],["Le zone sull'Equatore","Les zones sur l'équateur","Areas on the Equator"]],"e":["La Germania, come il nord della Francia, è vicina ai poli e ha un clima fresco.","L'Allemagne, comme le nord de la France, est proche des pôles et a un climat frais.","Germany, like northern France, lies nearer the poles and has a cool climate."],"d":["Le regioni a clima fresco sono quelle più vicine ai poli, come la Germania e il nord della Francia. Alcune parti dell'Australia e della California sono invece esempi di clima caldo. Vicino all'Equatore fa troppo caldo perché la vite cresca bene e possa riposare in inverno.","Les régions de climat frais sont les plus proches des pôles, comme l'Allemagne et le nord de la France. Certaines parties de l'Australie et de la Californie sont au contraire des exemples de climat chaud. Près de l'équateur, il fait trop chaud pour que la vigne pousse bien et se repose en hiver.","Cool climate regions are those closer to the poles, such as Germany and northern France. Parts of Australia and California are examples of warm climates instead. Right at the Equator it is too hot for vines to grow well and rest in winter."]},{"id":"l1535aca1","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Quale tipo di uva si coltiva più spesso nelle regioni a clima caldo?","Quel type de raisin cultive-t-on le plus souvent dans les régions chaudes ?","Which type of grape is commonly grown in warm climate regions?"],"o":[["Le uve nere","Les raisins noirs","Black grapes"],["Le uve bianche","Les raisins blancs","White grapes"],["Le uve acerbe","Les raisins verts","Unripe grapes"],["Le uve senza buccia","Les raisins sans peau","Skinless grapes"]],"e":["Nei climi caldi l'uva matura con regolarità ed è comune coltivare uve nere.","En climat chaud, le raisin mûrit régulièrement et on cultive souvent des raisins noirs.","Warm climates ripen grapes reliably, and black grapes are commonly grown."],"d":["Le regioni calde, più vicine all'Equatore, hanno temperature medie alte e un sole più intenso, quindi l'uva matura con regolarità. In queste zone è comune coltivare uve nere. Nelle regioni fresche, dove l'uva a volte fatica a maturare, è invece frequente coltivare uve bianche.","Les régions chaudes, plus proches de l'équateur, ont des températures moyennes élevées et un soleil plus intense ; le raisin y mûrit donc régulièrement. On y cultive souvent des raisins noirs. Dans les régions fraîches, où le raisin peine parfois à mûrir, on cultive plutôt des raisins blancs.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown."]},{"id":"l1c999a0b","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["In un clima fresco, come saranno di solito le uve?","En climat frais, comment seront généralement les raisins ?","In a cool climate, grapes will usually have…"],"o":[["Meno zucchero e più acidità","Moins de sucre et plus d'acidité","Less sugar and more acidity"],["Più zucchero e meno acidità","Plus de sucre et moins d'acidité","More sugar and less acidity"],["Più zucchero e più acidità","Plus de sucre et plus d'acidité","More sugar and more acidity"],["Meno zucchero e meno acidità","Moins de sucre et moins d'acidité","Less sugar and less acidity"]],"e":["Più fa fresco, più l'uva resta acida e meno zucchero accumula.","Plus il fait frais, plus le raisin reste acide et moins il accumule de sucre.","The cooler it is, the more acidic and less sugary the grapes stay."],"d":["Con poco calore e un sole più debole, l'uva matura meno: accumula meno zucchero e conserva più acidità. Il risultato nel bicchiere sono vini tendenzialmente più leggeri e freschi. In un clima caldo succede il contrario: più zucchero, meno acidità e sapori più maturi.","Avec peu de chaleur et un soleil plus faible, le raisin mûrit moins : il accumule moins de sucre et garde plus d'acidité. Dans le verre, cela donne des vins plutôt légers et frais. En climat chaud, c'est l'inverse : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité et des saveurs plus mûres.","With little heat and weaker sunshine, grapes ripen less: they build up less sugar and keep more acidity. In the glass this tends to give lighter, fresher wines. In a warm climate the opposite happens: more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours."]},{"id":"l115b6166","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché un vino da clima caldo tende ad avere sapori di frutta più maturi?","Pourquoi un vin de climat chaud a-t-il en général des saveurs de fruits plus mûres ?","Why does a warm-climate wine tend to show riper fruit flavours?"],"o":[["Il calore fa maturare di più l'uva","La chaleur fait davantage mûrir le raisin","Heat ripens the grapes further"],["Il calore aumenta l'acidità dell'uva","La chaleur augmente l'acidité du raisin","Heat raises the grapes' acidity"],["Il calore toglie colore alle bucce","La chaleur enlève la couleur des peaux","Heat removes colour from the skins"],["Il calore ferma la fioritura","La chaleur arrête la floraison","Heat stops the vine flowering"]],"e":["Con più calore e sole l'uva matura di più: più zucchero, sapori più maturi.","Avec plus de chaleur et de soleil, le raisin mûrit davantage : plus de sucre, saveurs plus mûres.","More heat and sun ripen grapes further: more sugar, riper flavours."],"d":["Nelle regioni calde le temperature medie sono alte e il sole è intenso, quindi l'uva matura con regolarità e a fondo. Questo porta più zucchero, meno acidità e sapori più maturi. Lo Chardonnay, per esempio, passa dai profumi di mela e limone in clima fresco a pesca e ananas in clima caldo.","Dans les régions chaudes, les températures moyennes sont élevées et le soleil est intense ; le raisin mûrit donc régulièrement et pleinement. Cela donne plus de sucre, moins d'acidité et des saveurs plus mûres. Le Chardonnay, par exemple, passe de la pomme et du citron en climat frais à la pêche et à l'ananas en climat chaud.","In warm regions average temperatures are high and the sunshine is intense, so grapes ripen fully and reliably. This brings more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours. Chardonnay, for example, moves from apple and lemon aromas in a cool climate to peach and pineapple in a warm one."]},{"id":"l1025d685","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Uno Chardonnay con profumi di mela e limone viene probabilmente da…","Un Chardonnay aux arômes de pomme et de citron vient probablement…","A Chardonnay with apple and lemon aromas most likely comes from…"],"o":[["Un clima fresco","D'un climat frais","A cool climate"],["Un clima caldo","D'un climat chaud","A warm climate"],["Un clima tropicale","D'un climat tropical","A tropical climate"],["Un clima molto secco","D'un climat très sec","A very dry climate"]],"e":["Frutta verde e agrumi indicano uva meno matura, tipica del clima fresco.","Fruits verts et agrumes signalent un raisin moins mûr, typique du climat frais.","Green fruit and citrus point to less ripe, cool-climate grapes."],"d":["Il clima cambia il tipo di frutta che si sente nel vino. In clima fresco lo Chardonnay dà frutta verde come la mela e agrumi come il limone. In clima caldo, con uva più matura, mostra frutta a nocciolo come la pesca e frutta tropicale come l'ananas.","Le climat change le type de fruits que l'on perçoit dans le vin. En climat frais, le Chardonnay donne des fruits verts comme la pomme et des agrumes comme le citron. En climat chaud, avec un raisin plus mûr, il montre des fruits à noyau comme la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas.","Climate changes the type of fruit you find in a wine. In a cool climate Chardonnay gives green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. In a warm climate, with riper grapes, it shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple."]},{"id":"l19fd4d7a","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Perché nelle regioni a clima fresco l'uva, in certe annate, fatica a maturare?","Pourquoi, dans les régions fraîches, le raisin a-t-il parfois du mal à mûrir ?","Why can grapes in cool regions struggle to ripen in some years?"],"o":[["Temperature basse e sole più debole","Températures basses et soleil plus faible","Low temperatures and weaker sunlight"],["Temperature alte e sole più intenso","Températures élevées et soleil plus intense","High temperatures and stronger sunlight"],["Inverni troppo miti per riposare","Hivers trop doux pour se reposer","Winters too mild for the vine to rest"],["Viti troppo giovani per fiorire","Vignes trop jeunes pour fleurir","Vines too young to flower"]],"e":["Poco calore e luce più debole rallentano la maturazione dell'uva.","Peu de chaleur et une lumière plus faible ralentissent la maturation du raisin.","Little heat and weaker light slow down ripening."],"d":["Le regioni fresche sono più vicine ai poli: le temperature medie sono basse e la luce del sole può essere meno intensa che vicino all'Equatore. In annate particolarmente fresche l'uva può non maturare del tutto. Per questo in queste zone si coltivano spesso uve bianche.","Les régions fraîches sont plus proches des pôles : les températures moyennes y sont basses et la lumière du soleil peut être moins intense que près de l'équateur. Les années particulièrement fraîches, le raisin peut ne pas mûrir complètement. C'est pourquoi on y cultive souvent des raisins blancs.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there."]},{"id":"l1ecdb47c","c":"p1","p":0,"q":["Dopo l'impianto, quanto tempo serve in genere perché una vite dia un raccolto ogni anno?","Après la plantation, combien de temps faut-il en général pour qu'une vigne donne une récolte chaque année ?","After planting, how long does a vine usually take before it gives a crop every year?"],"o":[["Un paio d'anni","Environ deux ans","A couple of years"],["Pochi mesi","Quelques mois","A few months"],["Circa vent'anni","Environ vingt ans","About twenty years"],["Mezzo secolo","Un demi-siècle","Half a century"]],"e":["Una vite diventa adulta un paio d'anni dopo l'impianto, poi produce ogni anno.","Une vigne devient adulte environ deux ans après la plantation, puis produit chaque année.","A vine matures a couple of years after planting, then crops every year."],"d":["La vite è una pianta longeva, che può vivere per diversi decenni. Dopo l'impianto le servono un paio d'anni per diventare adulta; da quel momento produce un raccolto di uva ogni anno, seguendo sempre lo stesso ciclo: fioritura in primavera, maturazione in estate e vendemmia a fine estate.","La vigne est une plante qui vit longtemps, parfois plusieurs dizaines d'années. Après la plantation, il lui faut environ deux ans pour arriver à maturité ; elle donne ensuite une récolte chaque année, en suivant toujours le même cycle : floraison au printemps, maturation en été et vendanges en fin d'été.","The vine is a long-lived plant that can survive for several decades. After planting it needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year, always following the same cycle: flowering in spring, ripening in summer and harvest in late summer."]},{"id":"l1a9bcaeb","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale tipo di vino ha ricevuto un'aggiunta di alcol?","Quel type de vin a reçu un ajout d'alcool ?","Which type of wine has had extra alcohol added?"],"o":[["Fortificato","Fortifié","Fortified"],["Spumante","Effervescent","Sparkling"],["Fermo","Tranquille","Still"],["Rosato","Rosé","Rosé"]],"e":["Nei vini fortificati si aggiunge alcol, per questo sono più forti.","On ajoute de l'alcool aux vins fortifiés, d'où leur degré plus élevé.","Fortified wines have alcohol added, which makes them stronger."],"d":["Esistono tre tipi di vino: fermo, spumante e fortificato. Solo il fortificato riceve un'aggiunta di alcol, che porta il grado tra il 15% e il 22% vol. Lo spumante deve le bollicine all'anidride carbonica della fermentazione, mentre il rosato è un colore, non un tipo di vino.","Il existe trois types de vin : tranquille, effervescent et fortifié. Seul le fortifié reçoit un ajout d'alcool, qui porte son degré entre 15 % et 22 % vol. L'effervescent doit ses bulles au dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation, et le rosé est une couleur, pas un type de vin.","There are three types of wine: still, sparkling and fortified. Only fortified wine has extra alcohol added, which lifts it to between 15% and 22% abv. Sparkling wine owes its bubbles to carbon dioxide from fermentation, and rosé is a colour, not a type of wine."]},{"id":"l179538c6","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Qual è la gradazione tipica dei vini fortificati?","Quel est le degré habituel des vins fortifiés ?","What is the usual alcohol range of fortified wines?"],"o":[["15–22% vol.","15–22 % vol.","15–22% abv"],["8–11% vol.","8–11 % vol.","8–11% abv"],["11,5–14% vol.","11,5–14 % vol.","11.5–14% abv"],["4–7% vol.","4–7 % vol.","4–7% abv"]],"e":["L'alcol aggiunto porta i fortificati tra il 15% e il 22% vol.","L'alcool ajouté place les fortifiés entre 15 % et 22 % vol.","The added alcohol puts fortified wines between 15% and 22% abv."],"d":["I vini fermi e spumanti stanno quasi sempre tra l'11,5% e il 14% vol., con estremi tra 8% e 15%. I fortificati, come Sherry e Port, ricevono alcol in più e salgono a una fascia più alta, tra il 15% e il 22% vol.","Les vins tranquilles et effervescents se situent presque toujours entre 11,5 % et 14 % vol., avec des extrêmes de 8 % à 15 %. Les fortifiés, comme le Sherry et le Port, reçoivent de l'alcool en plus et montent dans une fourchette plus haute, de 15 % à 22 % vol.","Still and sparkling wines almost always sit between 11.5% and 14% abv, with extremes from 8% to 15%. Fortified wines such as Sherry and Port have extra alcohol added, so they move up into a higher band of 15% to 22% abv."]},{"id":"l107426b9","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Da dove vengono le bollicine di un vino spumante?","D'où viennent les bulles d'un vin effervescent ?","Where do the bubbles in sparkling wine come from?"],"o":[["Anidride carbonica della fermentazione rimasta nel vino","Dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation resté dans le vin","Carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine"],["Alcol distillato aggiunto dopo la fermentazione","Alcool distillé ajouté après la fermentation","Distilled alcohol added after fermentation"],["Zucchero lasciato nel vino dopo la fermentazione","Sucre laissé dans le vin après la fermentation","Sugar left in the wine after fermentation"],["Aria che entra dalle doghe delle botti","Air qui entre par les douelles des fûts","Air entering through the oak barrel staves"]],"e":["La fermentazione produce anidride carbonica; se resta intrappolata, forma le bollicine.","La fermentation produit du dioxyde de carbone ; piégé, il forme les bulles.","Fermentation makes carbon dioxide; when it is trapped, it becomes the bubbles."],"d":["I lieviti trasformano lo zucchero in alcol e anidride carbonica. Nei vini fermi il gas si disperde nell'aria, mentre negli spumanti viene trattenuto nel vino. Quando si apre la bottiglia, il gas si libera sotto forma di bollicine, come nello Champagne, nel Cava o nel Prosecco.","Les levures transforment le sucre en alcool et en dioxyde de carbone. Dans les vins tranquilles, le gaz s'échappe dans l'air ; dans les effervescents, il est retenu dans le vin. À l'ouverture de la bouteille, il se libère sous forme de bulles, comme dans le Champagne, le Cava ou le Prosecco.","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. In still wines the gas escapes into the air, but in sparkling wines it is kept inside the wine. When the bottle is opened, the gas is released as bubbles, as in Champagne, Cava or Prosecco."]},{"id":"l1971e121","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Tra quali valori si trova la maggior parte dei vini fermi?","Entre quelles valeurs se situent la plupart des vins tranquilles ?","Between which values do most still wines fall?"],"o":[["11,5% e 14% vol.","11,5 % et 14 % vol.","11.5% and 14% abv"],["15% e 22% vol.","15 % et 22 % vol.","15% and 22% abv"],["5% e 8% vol.","5 % et 8 % vol.","5% and 8% abv"],["16% e 20% vol.","16 % et 20 % vol.","16% and 20% abv"]],"e":["I vini fermi vanno da 8% a 15% vol., ma quasi tutti stanno tra 11,5% e 14%.","Les tranquilles vont de 8 % à 15 % vol., mais presque tous entre 11,5 % et 14 %.","Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, but most sit between 11.5% and 14%."],"d":["La fascia completa dei vini fermi va dall'8% al 15% vol., ma la grande maggioranza si colloca tra l'11,5% e il 14%. Valori tra il 15% e il 22% sono tipici dei vini fortificati, a cui si aggiunge alcol. Un vino come il White Zinfandel è un esempio di gradazione bassa.","La fourchette complète des vins tranquilles va de 8 % à 15 % vol., mais la grande majorité se situe entre 11,5 % et 14 %. Les valeurs de 15 % à 22 % sont typiques des vins fortifiés, auxquels on ajoute de l'alcool. Le White Zinfandel est un exemple de vin peu alcoolisé.","The full range for still wines runs from 8% to 15% abv, but the great majority sit between 11.5% and 14%. Figures of 15% to 22% are typical of fortified wines, which have alcohol added. White Zinfandel is an example of a still wine at the low end."]},{"id":"l1e094933","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini prende il nome dal vitigno?","Lequel de ces vins porte le nom de son cépage ?","Which of these wines is named after its grape variety?"],"o":[["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Rioja","Rioja","Rioja"],["Chianti","Chianti","Chianti"],["Sancerre","Sancerre","Sancerre"]],"e":["Pinot Grigio è un vitigno; Rioja, Chianti e Sancerre sono zone di produzione.","Pinot Grigio est un cépage ; Rioja, Chianti et Sancerre sont des régions.","Pinot Grigio is a grape; Rioja, Chianti and Sancerre are places."],"d":["Molti vini europei portano il nome della zona in cui sono prodotti: Rioja in Spagna, Chianti in Italia, Sancerre in Francia. Altri vini, invece, indicano in etichetta il vitigno usato. Il Pinot Grigio è proprio un esempio di vino chiamato con il nome dell'uva.","Beaucoup de vins européens portent le nom de leur région de production : Rioja en Espagne, Chianti en Italie, Sancerre en France. D'autres indiquent plutôt le cépage sur l'étiquette. Le Pinot Grigio est justement un exemple de vin désigné par le nom de son raisin.","Many European wines take the name of the area where they are made: Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy, Sancerre in France. Other wines show the grape variety on the label instead. Pinot Grigio is a typical example of a wine named after its grape."]},{"id":"l1fc54261","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi è uno spumante spagnolo?","Lequel de ces vins est un effervescent espagnol ?","Which of these is a Spanish sparkling wine?"],"o":[["Cava","Cava","Cava"],["Prosecco","Prosecco","Prosecco"],["Champagne","Champagne","Champagne"],["Sherry","Sherry","Sherry"]],"e":["Il Cava è lo spumante della Spagna.","Le Cava est l'effervescent espagnol.","Cava is the sparkling wine from Spain."],"d":["Tre spumanti famosi da ricordare: Champagne dalla Francia, Prosecco dall'Italia e Cava dalla Spagna. Anche lo Sherry è spagnolo, ma è un vino fortificato, non uno spumante: ha ricevuto alcol in più e non ha bollicine. Gli spumanti, comunque, si producono oggi in quasi tutti i paesi del vino.","Trois effervescents célèbres à retenir : le Champagne de France, le Prosecco d'Italie et le Cava d'Espagne. Le Sherry est lui aussi espagnol, mais c'est un vin fortifié, pas un effervescent : il a reçu de l'alcool en plus et n'a pas de bulles. On produit d'ailleurs aujourd'hui des effervescents dans presque tous les pays viticoles.","Three famous sparkling wines to remember: Champagne from France, Prosecco from Italy and Cava from Spain. Sherry is also Spanish, but it is a fortified wine, not a sparkling one: it has had alcohol added and has no bubbles. Sparkling wines are, in fact, now made in almost every wine-producing country."]},{"id":"l1822e6c3","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Perché un vino rosso è rosso?","Pourquoi un vin rouge est-il rouge ?","Why is a red wine red?"],"o":[["Le bucce restano nel succo durante la fermentazione","Les peaux restent dans le jus pendant la fermentation","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation"],["La polpa delle uve nere è di colore rosso","La pulpe des raisins noirs est de couleur rouge","The pulp of black grapes is red in colour"],["Le botti di rovere cedono colore al vino","Les fûts de chêne donnent leur couleur au vin","The oak barrels give their colour to the wine"],["Si aggiunge succo d'uva nera non fermentato","On ajoute du jus de raisin noir non fermenté","Unfermented black grape juice is added"]],"e":["Il colore è nelle bucce, che cedono colore durante la fermentazione.","La couleur est dans les peaux, qui la cèdent pendant la fermentation.","The colour is in the skins, which release it during fermentation."],"d":["La polpa delle uve bianche e nere ha lo stesso colore e il succo è incolore. Per fare un rosso si usano uve nere e si lasciano le bucce a contatto con il succo per tutta la fermentazione, mescolando bene: così passano nel vino colore e tannino.","La pulpe des raisins blancs et noirs a la même couleur et le jus est incolore. Pour faire un rouge, on utilise des raisins noirs et on laisse les peaux au contact du jus pendant toute la fermentation, en mélangeant bien : couleur et tanins passent ainsi dans le vin.","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine."]},{"id":"l16e9106c","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Si può fare un vino bianco con uve nere?","Peut-on faire un vin blanc avec des raisins noirs ?","Can a white wine be made from black grapes?"],"o":[["Sì, separando le bucce dal succo prima della fermentazione","Oui, en séparant les peaux du jus avant la fermentation","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation"],["Sì, ma solo se il vino viene affinato in rovere","Oui, mais seulement si le vin est élevé en chêne","Yes, but only if the wine is then aged in oak"],["No, le uve nere danno sempre un vino rosso","Non, les raisins noirs donnent toujours du rouge","No, black grapes always give a red wine"],["No, le uve nere danno solo vini rosati","Non, les raisins noirs ne donnent que du rosé","No, black grapes can only make rosé wine"]],"e":["Il succo delle uve nere è incolore: senza bucce, il vino resta bianco.","Le jus des raisins noirs est incolore : sans les peaux, le vin reste blanc.","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white."],"d":["Il colore delle uve nere si trova solo nella buccia. Se le uve vengono pressate delicatamente e le bucce separate dal succo prima della fermentazione, il succo resta chiaro e dà un vino bianco. È lo stesso principio che permette di usare il Pinot Noir nello Champagne.","La couleur des raisins noirs se trouve uniquement dans la peau. Si l'on presse les raisins doucement et qu'on sépare les peaux du jus avant la fermentation, le jus reste clair et donne un vin blanc. C'est ce principe qui permet d'utiliser le Pinot Noir dans le Champagne.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne."]},{"id":"l18b7549f","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Come si ottiene un vino rosato?","Comment obtient-on un vin rosé ?","How is a rosé wine made?"],"o":[["Uve nere, contatto con le bucce di poche ore","Raisins noirs, contact avec les peaux de quelques heures","Black grapes with only a few hours of skin contact"],["Uve bianche fermentate insieme alle loro bucce","Raisins blancs fermentés avec leurs peaux","White grapes fermented together with their skins"],["Uve nere con bucce fino a fine fermentazione","Raisins noirs avec peaux jusqu'à la fin de la fermentation","Black grapes kept on skins until fermentation ends"],["Uve bianche affinate a lungo in botti di rovere","Raisins blancs élevés longtemps en fût de chêne","White grapes aged for a long time in oak barrels"]],"e":["Il succo resta poche ore con le bucce di uve nere, poi viene separato.","Le jus reste quelques heures avec les peaux de raisins noirs, puis il est écoulé.","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off."],"d":["Il rosato nasce da uve nere, come il rosso, ma il contatto con le bucce dura solo qualche ora. Il succo, appena rosa, viene separato e termina la fermentazione senza bucce. Se invece le bucce restassero fino alla fine, si otterrebbe un vino rosso.","Le rosé naît de raisins noirs, comme le rouge, mais le contact avec les peaux ne dure que quelques heures. Le jus, à peine rose, est écoulé et termine sa fermentation sans les peaux. Si les peaux restaient jusqu'à la fin, on obtiendrait un vin rouge.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead."]},{"id":"l11609a42","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini è un rosato?","Lequel de ces vins est un rosé ?","Which of these wines is a rosé?"],"o":[["White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel"],["Chablis","Chablis","Chablis"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Sauternes","Sauternes","Sauternes"]],"e":["Nonostante il nome, il White Zinfandel della California è un rosato.","Malgré son nom, le White Zinfandel de Californie est un rosé.","Despite its name, White Zinfandel from California is a rosé."],"d":["Il nome può ingannare: il White Zinfandel è un rosato californiano, di dolcezza media, poco alcolico e con fragola e lampone. Lo Chablis e il Sauternes sono vini bianchi francesi, mentre il Beaujolais è un rosso leggero e poco tannico. Ricorda di non giudicare un vino solo dal nome.","Le nom peut tromper : le White Zinfandel est un rosé californien, demi-doux, peu alcoolisé, aux arômes de fraise et de framboise. Le Chablis et le Sauternes sont des blancs français, tandis que le Beaujolais est un rouge léger et peu tannique. Mieux vaut donc ne jamais juger un vin à son seul nom.","The name can mislead you: White Zinfandel is a Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry flavours. Chablis and Sauternes are French white wines, while Beaujolais is a light red with low tannin. So never judge a wine by its name alone."]},{"id":"l11970f5b","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede quando si fa un vino secco?","Que se passe-t-il quand on fait un vin sec ?","What happens when a dry wine is made?"],"o":[["I lieviti trasformano in alcol tutto lo zucchero","Les levures transforment tout le sucre en alcool","The yeast turn all of the sugar into alcohol"],["Si aggiunge alcol distillato prima della fine","On ajoute de l'alcool distillé avant la fin","Distilled alcohol is added before fermentation ends"],["Si aggiunge succo d'uva non fermentato","On ajoute du jus de raisin non fermenté","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine"],["Si tolgono i lieviti prima della fine","On retire les levures avant la fin","The yeast are removed before they finish"]],"e":["Un vino è secco quando i lieviti hanno consumato tutto lo zucchero.","Un vin est sec quand les levures ont consommé tout le sucre.","A wine is dry when the yeast have eaten all the sugar."],"d":["La maggior parte dei vini è secca: i lieviti continuano a lavorare finché non hanno trasformato tutto lo zucchero in alcol. Le altre risposte descrivono come si ottengono vini con zucchero residuo: togliere i lieviti o aggiungere succo per i vini medi, aggiungere alcol per i fortificati dolci.","La plupart des vins sont secs : les levures travaillent jusqu'à avoir transformé tout le sucre en alcool. Les autres réponses décrivent des façons de garder du sucre : retirer les levures ou ajouter du jus pour les demi-doux, ajouter de l'alcool pour les fortifiés doux.","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines."]},{"id":"l137e18b3","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale metodo serve a ottenere un vino di dolcezza media?","Quelle méthode permet d'obtenir un vin demi-doux ?","Which method is used to make a medium-sweet wine?"],"o":[["Aggiungere succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco","Ajouter du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine"],["Lasciare le bucce nel succo per più tempo","Laisser les peaux plus longtemps dans le jus","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer"],["Far affinare il vino in botti di rovere","Élever le vin en fût de chêne","Maturing the wine in oak barrels"],["Raccogliere l'uva prima che maturi","Vendanger le raisin avant sa maturité","Picking the grapes before they ripen"]],"e":["Il succo non fermentato aggiunge zucchero a un vino già secco.","Le jus non fermenté apporte du sucre à un vin déjà sec.","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine."],"d":["Per i vini di dolcezza media ci sono due strade: togliere i lieviti prima che abbiano consumato tutto lo zucchero, oppure aggiungere succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco. Bucce e rovere influiscono su colore, tannino e aromi, non sulla dolcezza.","Pour les vins demi-doux, il y a deux voies : retirer les levures avant qu'elles aient consommé tout le sucre, ou ajouter du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec. Les peaux et le chêne influencent la couleur, les tanins et les arômes, pas la sucrosité.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness."]},{"id":"l13e6e934","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["In un vino fortificato dolce, che cosa ferma la fermentazione?","Dans un vin fortifié doux, qu'est-ce qui arrête la fermentation ?","In a sweet fortified wine, what stops the fermentation?"],"o":[["L'aggiunta di alcol distillato che uccide i lieviti","L'ajout d'alcool distillé qui tue les levures","Adding distilled alcohol, which kills the yeast"],["L'aggiunta di succo d'uva non fermentato","L'ajout de jus de raisin non fermenté","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine"],["Il passaggio in botti di rovere","Le passage en fût de chêne","Moving the wine into oak barrels"],["La separazione del vino dalle bucce","La séparation du vin et des peaux","Draining the wine off the skins"]],"e":["L'alcol forte aggiunto uccide i lieviti e lascia zucchero nel vino.","L'alcool fort ajouté tue les levures et laisse du sucre dans le vin.","The strong added alcohol kills the yeast, leaving sugar in the wine."],"d":["Nei fortificati dolci si aggiunge alcol distillato ad alta gradazione prima che i lieviti abbiano consumato tutto lo zucchero. I lieviti muoiono, lo zucchero rimasto rende il vino dolce e l'alcol aggiunto lo rende più forte. È il caso del Port e di alcuni Sherry.","Dans les fortifiés doux, on ajoute un alcool distillé très fort avant que les levures aient consommé tout le sucre. Les levures meurent, le sucre restant rend le vin doux et l'alcool ajouté le rend plus fort. C'est le cas du Port et de certains Sherry.","In sweet fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die, the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol makes it stronger. Port and some Sherries are made this way."]},{"id":"l1b49d626","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale sensazione indica un'acidità alta?","Quelle sensation révèle une acidité élevée ?","Which sensation tells you a wine has high acidity?"],"o":[["Fa venire l'acquolina in bocca","Elle fait saliver","It makes your mouth water"],["Lascia la bocca asciutta","Elle assèche la bouche","It makes your mouth feel dry"],["Dà calore in gola","Elle chauffe la gorge","It warms the back of your throat"],["Sembra densa e sciropposa","Elle paraît épaisse et sirupeuse","It feels thick and syrupy"]],"e":["L'acidità si riconosce perché fa salivare.","On reconnaît l'acidité au fait qu'elle fait saliver.","Acidity is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water."],"d":["Ogni elemento della struttura si riconosce da una sensazione diversa. L'acidità fa salivare e dà freschezza. Il tannino, invece, asciuga la bocca; l'alcol si percepisce come calore; un vino molto dolce può sembrare denso e sciropposo. Troppa acidità, però, rende il vino sgradevolmente aspro.","Chaque élément de la structure se reconnaît à une sensation différente. L'acidité fait saliver et apporte de la fraîcheur. Le tanin, lui, assèche la bouche ; l'alcool se perçoit comme une chaleur ; un vin très doux peut paraître épais et sirupeux. Trop d'acidité rend toutefois le vin désagréablement acide.","Each part of a wine's structure has its own sensation. Acidity makes your mouth water and brings freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth; alcohol is felt as warmth; and a very sweet wine can feel thick and syrupy. Too much acidity, however, makes a wine taste unpleasantly sharp."]},{"id":"l16964d99","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Perché l'acidità è importante nei vini dolci?","Pourquoi l'acidité est-elle importante dans les vins doux ?","Why is acidity important in sweet wines?"],"o":[["Bilancia la dolcezza e evita che il vino stanchi","Elle équilibre la douceur et évite l'écœurement","It balances the sweetness so the wine is not cloying"],["Aumenta il grado alcolico del vino","Elle augmente le degré d'alcool du vin","It raises the alcohol level of the wine"],["Dà al vino un colore più intenso","Elle donne au vin une couleur plus intense","It gives the wine a deeper colour"],["Aggiunge tannino e quindi più corpo","Elle ajoute du tanin et donc du corps","It adds tannin and therefore more body"]],"e":["Senza acidità un vino dolce risulterebbe stucchevole.","Sans acidité, un vin doux serait écœurant.","Without acidity, a sweet wine would taste cloying."],"d":["L'acidità viene dal succo d'uva e rinfresca il vino. Nei vini dolci fa da contrappeso allo zucchero: per questo il Sauternes e i Riesling dolci hanno un'acidità alta. Non influisce su colore, tannino o grado alcolico. Senza di essa il vino sembrerebbe pesante.","L'acidité vient du jus de raisin et rafraîchit le vin. Dans les vins doux, elle fait contrepoids au sucre : c'est pourquoi le Sauternes et les Riesling doux ont une acidité élevée. Elle n'agit ni sur la couleur, ni sur les tanins, ni sur le degré. Sans elle, le vin paraîtrait lourd.","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy."]},{"id":"l14d484db","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Da dove proviene il tannino del vino?","D'où vient le tanin du vin ?","Where does tannin in wine come from?"],"o":[["Dalle bucce delle uve nere","De la peau des raisins noirs","The skins of black grapes"],["Dalla polpa delle uve bianche","De la pulpe des raisins blancs","The pulp of white grapes"],["Dallo zucchero del succo","Du sucre du jus","The sugar in the juice"],["Dai lieviti della fermentazione","Des levures de fermentation","The yeast used in fermentation"]],"e":["Il tannino si trova nelle bucce delle uve nere ed è tipico dei rossi.","Le tanin se trouve dans la peau des raisins noirs ; il est typique des rouges.","Tannin sits in black grape skins, which is why it is a red-wine feature."],"d":["Le uve nere hanno bucce colorate che contengono tannini. Durante la fermentazione dei rossi le bucce restano nel succo e cedono colore e tannino. Quanto tannino avrà il vino dipende dal vitigno e dalla vinificazione: ne ha molto il Bordeaux rosso, poco il Beaujolais.","Les raisins noirs ont une peau colorée qui contient des tanins. Pendant la fermentation des rouges, les peaux restent dans le jus et cèdent couleur et tanins. La quantité finale dépend du cépage et de la vinification : beaucoup dans le Bordeaux rouge, peu dans le Beaujolais.","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little."]},{"id":"l18f8a4b7","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi rossi ha poco tannino?","Lequel de ces rouges a peu de tanins ?","Which of these reds is low in tannin?"],"o":[["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Bordeaux rosso","Bordeaux rouge","Red Bordeaux"],["Chianti","Chianti","Chianti"],["Port","Port","Port"]],"e":["Il Beaujolais è un rosso leggero, fresco e poco tannico.","Le Beaujolais est un rouge léger, frais et peu tannique.","Beaujolais is a light, fresh red with low tannin."],"d":["Il Beaujolais è un esempio classico di rosso poco tannico, insieme ad alcuni Pinot Noir. Il Bordeaux rosso e il Chianti, invece, sono citati come rossi molto tannici, e anche il Port, vino fortificato rosso e dolce, ha tannini alti. Ricorda che il tannino lascia la bocca asciutta.","Le Beaujolais est un exemple classique de rouge peu tannique, comme certains Pinot Noir. Le Bordeaux rouge et le Chianti sont au contraire cités comme des rouges très tanniques, et le Port, vin fortifié rouge et doux, a lui aussi des tanins élevés. Rappel : le tanin assèche la bouche.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry."]},{"id":"l1076240a","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini è un esempio di vino molto alcolico?","Lequel de ces vins est un exemple de vin riche en alcool ?","Which of these is an example of a high-alcohol wine?"],"o":[["Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape"],["White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel","White Zinfandel"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"]],"e":["Lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape è un rosso francese pieno e ricco di alcol.","Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape est un rouge français corsé et riche en alcool.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a full-bodied French red with high alcohol."],"d":["Lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rosso del Rodano, è il classico esempio di vino ad alta gradazione: secco, di corpo pieno, con fragola e chiodi di garofano. All'opposto il White Zinfandel è citato come vino poco alcolico; Beaujolais e Pinot Grigio sono vini leggeri.","Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rouge de la vallée du Rhône, est l'exemple type du vin riche en alcool : sec, corsé, avec fraise et clou de girofle. À l'opposé, le White Zinfandel est cité comme vin peu alcoolisé ; Beaujolais et Pinot Grigio sont des vins légers.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a red from the Rhône, is the textbook example of a high-alcohol wine: dry and full-bodied, with strawberry and clove. At the other end, White Zinfandel is the standard low-alcohol example, while Beaujolais and Pinot Grigio are light-bodied wines."]},{"id":"l157bd02d","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa «12% vol.» in etichetta?","Que signifie « 12 % vol. » sur l'étiquette ?","What does «12% abv» on a label mean?"],"o":[["Il 12% del liquido è alcol","12 % du liquide est de l'alcool","12% of the liquid is alcohol"],["Il vino contiene il 12% di zucchero","Le vin contient 12 % de sucre","The wine contains 12% sugar"],["Il 12% delle uve era nero","12 % des raisins étaient noirs","12% of the grapes were black"],["Il vino ha passato 12 mesi in botte","Le vin a passé 12 mois en fût","The wine spent 12 months in oak"]],"e":["La percentuale in volume indica quanta parte del vino è alcol.","Le pourcentage en volume indique la part d'alcool dans le vin.","Alcohol by volume shows what share of the wine is alcohol."],"d":["Il grado alcolico si misura come percentuale in volume (abv in inglese). Un vino a 12% vol. contiene dodici parti di alcol su cento. È un valore tipico di un vino fermo: la maggior parte si colloca tra l'11,5% e il 14%.","Le degré d'alcool se mesure en pourcentage du volume (abv en anglais). Un vin à 12 % vol. contient douze parts d'alcool sur cent. C'est une valeur typique d'un vin tranquille : la plupart se situent entre 11,5 % et 14 %.","Alcohol is measured as a percentage of the total volume, called alcohol by volume or abv. A wine at 12% abv has twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. That is a typical figure for a still wine, as most sit between 11.5% and 14%."]},{"id":"l129fb223","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cosa descrive il corpo di un vino?","Que décrit le corps d'un vin ?","What does the body of a wine describe?"],"o":[["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche","How mouth-filling the wine feels"],["Quanta acidità contiene il vino","Combien d'acidité contient le vin","How much acidity the wine contains"],["Quanto è intenso il colore del vino","L'intensité de la couleur du vin","How deep the colour of the wine is"],["Quanto tempo è rimasto in botte","Combien de temps il est resté en fût","How long the wine stayed in oak"]],"e":["Il corpo è la sensazione generale in bocca: leggero, medio o pieno.","Le corps est la sensation globale en bouche : léger, moyen ou corsé.","Body is the overall feel in the mouth: light, medium or full."],"d":["Il corpo dipende da molti fattori, quindi la domanda pratica è: quanto riempie la bocca questo vino? I vini pieni, come Sauternes o un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano, sembrano densi e avvolgenti; quelli leggeri, come Pinot Grigio e Beaujolais, più delicati.","Le corps dépend de nombreux facteurs, d'où la question pratique : à quel point ce vin remplit-il la bouche ? Les vins corsés, comme le Sauternes ou un Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie, paraissent denses ; les vins légers, comme le Pinot Grigio et le Beaujolais, plus délicats.","Many factors shape body, so the practical question is: how much does this wine fill my mouth? Full-bodied wines such as Sauternes or a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon feel dense and rich, while light ones such as Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais feel more delicate."]},{"id":"l14c942e8","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi vini ha corpo pieno?","Lequel de ces vins est corsé ?","Which of these wines is full-bodied?"],"o":[["Sauternes","Sauternes","Sauternes"],["Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio","Pinot Grigio"],["Beaujolais","Beaujolais","Beaujolais"],["Sancerre","Sancerre","Sancerre"]],"e":["Il Sauternes, bianco dolce di Bordeaux, ha corpo pieno.","Le Sauternes, blanc doux de Bordeaux, est corsé.","Sauternes, the sweet white from Bordeaux, is full-bodied."],"d":["Il Sauternes è dolce e di corpo pieno, con albicocca, miele e vaniglia. Il Pinot Grigio e il Beaujolais sono esempi di vini di corpo leggero, mentre il Sancerre è un bianco secco di corpo medio. Anche un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano sarebbe un buon esempio di vino pieno.","Le Sauternes est doux et corsé, avec abricot, miel et vanille. Le Pinot Grigio et le Beaujolais sont des exemples de vins légers, tandis que le Sancerre est un blanc sec de corps moyen. Un Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie serait lui aussi un bon exemple de vin corsé.","Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are examples of light-bodied wines, and Sancerre is a dry white with medium body. A Californian Cabernet Sauvignon would also be a good example of a full-bodied wine."]},{"id":"l10adad8b","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale gruppo di aromi deriva tipicamente dal rovere?","Quel groupe d'arômes vient en général du chêne ?","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?"],"o":[["Vaniglia, cedro, affumicato","Vanille, cèdre, fumé","Vanilla, cedar, smoke"],["Mela, limone, pera","Pomme, citron, poire","Apple, lemon, pear"],["Erba, asparago, peperone","Herbe, asperge, poivron","Grass, asparagus, bell pepper"],["Fragola, lampone, ciliegia","Fraise, framboise, cerise","Strawberry, raspberry, cherry"]],"e":["Il rovere dà vaniglia, cedro, affumicato, cocco e chiodi di garofano.","Le chêne apporte vanille, cèdre, fumé, noix de coco et clou de girofle.","Oak gives vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves."],"d":["Quando un vino fermenta o si affina in botti di rovere, il legno aggiunge note di vaniglia, cedro, affumicato, cocco e chiodi di garofano. Mela, limone e pera sono aromi di frutta; erba, asparago e peperone sono note erbacee tipiche, per esempio, del Sauvignon Blanc.","Quand un vin fermente ou s'élève en fût de chêne, le bois apporte des notes de vanille, de cèdre, de fumé, de noix de coco et de clou de girofle. Pomme, citron et poire sont des arômes de fruit ; herbe, asperge et poivron sont des notes herbacées typiques du Sauvignon Blanc.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, the wood adds notes of vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves. Apple, lemon and pear are fruit aromas, while grass, asparagus and bell pepper are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc, for example."]},{"id":"l14ebd294","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi ha di solito uno Chardonnay di clima fresco?","Quels arômes a en général un Chardonnay de climat frais ?","Which aromas does a cool-climate Chardonnay usually show?"],"o":[["Mela verde e limone","Pomme verte et citron","Green apple and lemon"],["Pesca e ananas","Pêche et ananas","Peach and pineapple"],["Ribes nero e menta","Cassis et menthe","Blackcurrant and mint"],["Fragola e ciliegia","Fraise et cerise","Strawberry and cherry"]],"e":["Nel clima fresco le uve maturano meno: frutta verde e agrumi.","En climat frais, le raisin mûrit moins : fruits verts et agrumes.","In a cool climate grapes ripen less, giving green fruit and citrus."],"d":["La maturità delle uve cambia il tipo di frutta che si sente. Uno Chardonnay di clima fresco profuma di mela verde e limone; uno di clima caldo di pesca e frutta tropicale come l'ananas. Ribes nero e menta sono tipici del Cabernet Sauvignon, fragola e ciliegia del Pinot Noir.","La maturité du raisin change le type de fruit perçu. Un Chardonnay de climat frais sent la pomme verte et le citron ; un Chardonnay de climat chaud, la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas. Cassis et menthe sont typiques du Cabernet Sauvignon, fraise et cerise du Pinot Noir.","How ripe the grapes are changes the fruit you notice. A cool-climate Chardonnay smells of green apple and lemon; a warm-climate one of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple. Blackcurrant and mint are typical of Cabernet Sauvignon, and strawberry and cherry of Pinot Noir."]},{"id":"l17f42e55","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi è un aroma della famiglia «altro»?","Lequel de ces arômes appartient à la famille « autres » ?","Which of these aromas belongs to the «other» family?"],"o":[["Funghi","Champignon","Mushroom"],["Ananas","Ananas","Pineapple"],["Vaniglia","Vanille","Vanilla"],["Ribes nero","Cassis","Blackcurrant"]],"e":["Funghi, terra, cuoio, erba e fiori rientrano negli «altri» aromi.","Champignon, terre, cuir, herbe et fleurs font partie des « autres » arômes.","Mushroom, earth, leather, grass and flowers are «other» aromas."],"d":["Gli aromi si dividono in tre famiglie: frutta, rovere e altro. Ananas e ribes nero sono frutta, la vaniglia viene dal rovere. Nella famiglia «altro» rientrano invece erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, ortaggi, terra, funghi e cuoio. Sono proprio questi aromi a rendere il vino così vario e interessante.","Les arômes se répartissent en trois familles : fruit, chêne et autres. L'ananas et le cassis sont des fruits, la vanille vient du chêne. La famille « autres » regroupe l'herbe, les fleurs, les herbes aromatiques, les légumes, la terre, le champignon et le cuir. Ce sont justement ces arômes qui rendent le vin si varié et passionnant.","Aromas fall into three families: fruit, oak and other. Pineapple and blackcurrant are fruit, and vanilla comes from oak. The «other» family covers grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. These are the aromas that make wine so varied and interesting to explore."]},{"id":"l1508807c","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è lo stile di un vino?","Qu'est-ce que le style d'un vin ?","What is the style of a wine?"],"o":[["L'insieme di colore, struttura e aromi","L'ensemble couleur, structure et arômes","Its colour, structure and aromas combined"],["Solo il vitigno con cui è fatto","Uniquement le cépage utilisé","Only the grape variety it is made from"],["Solo la zona in cui è prodotto","Uniquement la région de production","Only the region where it is produced"],["Solo il suo grado alcolico","Uniquement son degré d'alcool","Only its level of alcohol"]],"e":["Lo stile combina colore, struttura e aromi e sapori.","Le style combine couleur, structure, arômes et saveurs.","Style combines colour, structure, and aromas and flavours."],"d":["Vitigno, zona e alcol influenzano lo stile, ma da soli non lo descrivono. Lo stile è la somma di colore, struttura (dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo) e aromi e sapori. Per questo due bianchi francesi come Chablis e Sauternes possono avere stili opposti.","Le cépage, la région et l'alcool influencent le style, mais ne le décrivent pas à eux seuls. Le style est la somme de la couleur, de la structure (sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool, corps) et des arômes et saveurs. Deux blancs français comme le Chablis et le Sauternes peuvent donc s'opposer.","Grape, region and alcohol all influence style, but none of them describes it alone. Style is the sum of colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. That is how two French whites such as Chablis and Sauternes can be complete opposites."]},{"id":"l180fa384","c":"w1","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha un clima fresco sulle uve?","Quel effet a un climat frais sur le raisin ?","What effect does a cool climate have on the grapes?"],"o":[["Meno zucchero e più acidità","Moins de sucre et plus d'acidité","Less sugar and more acidity"],["Più zucchero e meno acidità","Plus de sucre et moins d'acidité","More sugar and less acidity"],["Più tannino e più colore","Plus de tanin et plus de couleur","More tannin and more colour"],["Sapori più maturi e tropicali","Des saveurs plus mûres et tropicales","Riper, more tropical flavours"]],"e":["Più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità hanno le uve.","Plus il fait frais, moins le raisin a de sucre et plus il a d'acidité.","The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acid the grapes have."],"d":["In generale, più il clima è fresco, più le uve restano acide e meno zuccherine; più è caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità, con sapori più maturi. Per questo i vini di clima fresco tendono a essere più freschi e leggeri, con frutta verde e agrumi.","En général, plus le climat est frais, plus le raisin reste acide et peu sucré ; plus il est chaud, plus il a de sucre et moins d'acidité, avec des saveurs plus mûres. C'est pourquoi les vins de climat frais sont souvent plus frais et légers, aux fruits verts et agrumes.","As a rule, the cooler the climate, the more acidic and the less sugary the grapes stay; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, with riper flavours. That is why cool-climate wines tend to be fresher and lighter, with green fruit and citrus."]}],"lessons":[{"c":"p1","t":["Com'è fatto un acino d'uva","Ce qu'il y a dans un grain de raisin","Inside a grape"],"p":[["Il vino nasce da un'idea semplice: si schiaccia l'uva, se ne libera il succo dolce e lo si lascia fermentare. Per questo il vino si può definire succo d'uva fermentato. Per capire che cosa finirà nel bicchiere conviene quindi partire dall'acino, che ha due parti principali: la buccia all'esterno e la polpa all'interno. Ognuna porta qualcosa di diverso al vino.","Le vin repose sur une idée simple : on écrase le raisin pour libérer son jus sucré, puis on le laisse fermenter. On peut donc définir le vin comme du jus de raisin fermenté. Pour comprendre ce que l'on trouvera dans le verre, il faut partir du grain de raisin, qui se compose de deux parties principales : la peau à l'extérieur et la pulpe à l'intérieur. Chacune apporte quelque chose de différent au vin.","Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine."],["Esistono due grandi famiglie di uve: bianche e nere. Tagliate a metà si somigliano molto, perché la differenza sta quasi tutta nella buccia. Le uve nere hanno una buccia dal colore intenso che contiene anche i tannini, sostanze che lasciano in bocca una sensazione di secchezza. Le uve bianche, a maturità, hanno invece una buccia di colore dorato.","Il existe deux grandes familles de raisins : blancs et noirs. Coupés en deux, ils se ressemblent beaucoup, car la différence se trouve surtout dans la peau. Les raisins noirs ont une peau très colorée qui contient aussi des tanins, des substances qui donnent une sensation de sécheresse en bouche. Les raisins blancs, une fois mûrs, ont une peau de couleur dorée.","There are two broad families of grapes: white and black. Cut in half, they look very much alike, because the real difference lies mainly in the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins that also hold tannins, substances that leave your mouth feeling dry. White grapes, once ripe, have skins with a golden colour."],["La polpa è la parte morbida e carnosa dell'acino e contiene il succo. Questo succo è formato soprattutto da acqua, zucchero e acido. Un dettaglio importante: il colore della polpa è lo stesso sia nelle uve bianche sia in quelle nere. Il colore di un vino rosso, quindi, non viene dal succo ma dalle bucce: è una chiave per capire più avanti come si fanno i diversi vini.","La pulpe est la partie tendre et charnue du grain ; c'est elle qui contient le jus. Ce jus est composé surtout d'eau, de sucre et d'acide. Détail important : la couleur de la pulpe est la même pour les raisins blancs et les raisins noirs. La couleur d'un vin rouge ne vient donc pas du jus mais des peaux, une clé pour comprendre plus tard comment on élabore les différents vins.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made."]],"k":[["Il vino è succo d'uva fermentato.","Le vin est du jus de raisin fermenté.","Wine is fermented grape juice."],["Buccia delle uve nere: colore intenso e tannini.","Peau des raisins noirs : couleur intense et tanins.","Black grape skins: deep colour and tannins."],["I tannini lasciano la bocca secca.","Les tanins assèchent la bouche.","Tannins make the mouth feel dry."],["Polpa: succo fatto di acqua, zucchero e acido.","Pulpe : jus fait d'eau, de sucre et d'acide.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid."],["La polpa ha lo stesso colore nelle uve bianche e nere.","La pulpe a la même couleur dans les raisins blancs et noirs.","Pulp is the same colour in white and black grapes."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["L'anno della vite","L'année de la vigne","The vine's year"],"p":[["L'uva è il frutto della vite, una pianta che può vivere per diversi decenni. Dopo l'impianto servono un paio d'anni perché la vite diventi adulta; da quel momento produce un raccolto ogni anno. Il suo ciclo segue le stagioni: fiorisce in primavera, i frutti maturano durante l'estate e la vendemmia arriva verso la fine dell'estate.","Le raisin est le fruit de la vigne, une plante qui peut vivre plusieurs dizaines d'années. Après la plantation, il faut environ deux ans pour que la vigne arrive à maturité ; elle donne ensuite une récolte chaque année. Son cycle suit les saisons : floraison au printemps, maturation des fruits pendant l'été et vendanges vers la fin de l'été.","Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. After planting, a vine needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year. Its cycle follows the seasons: it flowers in spring, the fruit ripens through the summer and the grapes are picked towards the end of summer."],["In primavera la vite produce grappoli di piccoli fiori. Ogni singolo fiore è destinato a trasformarsi in un acino. Subito dopo la fioritura gli acini appena formati sono piccoli, duri e verdi, sia che si tratti di uve bianche sia di uve nere: in questa fase non si distinguono ancora e non sono pronti per fare vino.","Au printemps, la vigne produit des grappes de petites fleurs. Chaque fleur est appelée à devenir un grain de raisin. Juste après la floraison, les jeunes grains sont petits, durs et verts, qu'il s'agisse de raisins blancs ou noirs : à ce stade, on ne peut pas encore les distinguer et ils ne sont pas prêts pour faire du vin.","In spring the vine produces clusters of tiny flowers. Each single flower is set to become one grape. Right after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, whether they will end up white or black: at this stage you cannot yet tell them apart, and they are far from ready to make wine."],["Perché la vite cresca bene e dia uva di qualità servono la giusta quantità di sole e di calore: se fa troppo freddo o troppo caldo non ci riesce. La vite preferisce inoltre zone con un inverno abbastanza freddo da permetterle di riposare. Per questo la maggior parte dei vigneti si trova in due fasce del pianeta, all'incirca tra i 30° e i 50° di latitudine, a nord e a sud dell'Equatore.","Pour bien pousser et donner des raisins de qualité, la vigne a besoin de la bonne dose de soleil et de chaleur : s'il fait trop froid ou trop chaud, elle n'y parvient pas. Elle préfère aussi les zones où l'hiver est assez froid pour lui permettre de se reposer. C'est pourquoi la plupart des vignobles se situent dans deux bandes du globe, à peu près entre 30° et 50° de latitude, au nord et au sud de l'équateur.","To grow well and give good quality fruit, a vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat: if it is too cold or too hot, it cannot manage. Vines also do best where the winter is cold enough to let them rest. That is why most vineyards lie in two bands around the globe, roughly between 30° and 50° of latitude, north and south of the Equator."]],"k":[["Una vite adulta dà un raccolto ogni anno e può vivere decenni.","Une vigne adulte donne une récolte par an et peut vivre des décennies.","A mature vine gives a crop every year and can live for decades."],["Primavera: fioritura; ogni fiore diventa un acino.","Printemps : floraison ; chaque fleur devient un grain.","Spring: flowering; each flower becomes a grape."],["Estate: maturazione; fine estate: vendemmia.","Été : maturation ; fin de l'été : vendanges.","Summer: ripening; late summer: harvest."],["La vite vuole sole e calore giusti e un inverno freddo per riposare.","La vigne veut assez de soleil et de chaleur et un hiver froid pour se reposer.","Vines need the right sun and heat, plus a cold winter to rest."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["Che cosa succede quando l'uva matura","Ce qui se passe quand le raisin mûrit","What happens as grapes ripen"],"p":[["Durante l'estate gli acini piccoli e duri cambiano profondamente. Si gonfiano perché si riempiono d'acqua, e allo stesso tempo il loro contenuto di zucchero sale mentre quello di acido scende. Anche i sapori evolvono e diventano più maturi. Un acino acerbo è quindi aspro e poco saporito, mentre un acino maturo è più grosso, più dolce e meno acido.","Pendant l'été, les petits grains durs changent profondément. Ils gonflent en se remplissant d'eau, tandis que leur teneur en sucre augmente et que leur teneur en acide diminue. Les saveurs évoluent elles aussi et deviennent plus mûres. Un raisin vert est donc acide et peu savoureux, alors qu'un raisin mûr est plus gros, plus sucré et moins acide.","Over the summer the small, hard grapes change a great deal. They swell as they fill with water, while their sugar content goes up and their acid content goes down. Their flavours also develop and become riper. An unripe grape is therefore sour and not very tasty, whereas a ripe grape is bigger, sweeter and less acidic."],["Con la maturazione cambia anche il colore della buccia. Le uve bianche passano dal verde a un colore dorato, mentre le uve nere passano dal verde al viola. Osservare il colore è quindi un primo indizio di quanto l'uva sia vicina alla vendemmia, insieme agli altri cambiamenti: più acqua, più zucchero, meno acido e sapori più maturi.","Avec la maturation, la couleur de la peau change aussi. Les raisins blancs passent du vert au doré, tandis que les raisins noirs passent du vert au violet. La couleur donne donc un premier indice sur la proximité des vendanges, en même temps que les autres changements : plus d'eau, plus de sucre, moins d'acide et des saveurs plus mûres.","Ripening also changes the colour of the skin. White grapes turn from green to golden, while black grapes turn from green to purple. Colour is therefore a first clue to how close the grapes are to harvest, alongside the other changes: more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours."],["Questi cambiamenti contano perché finiscono direttamente nel vino. Lo zucchero dell'uva è ciò che i lieviti trasformeranno in alcol: più zucchero significa, in genere, un vino più alcolico. L'acido resta nel vino e gli dà freschezza. I sapori dell'acino diventano gli aromi di frutta nel bicchiere. Il momento della vendemmia, quindi, orienta già lo stile del vino.","Ces changements comptent car ils passent directement dans le vin. Le sucre du raisin est ce que les levures transformeront en alcool : plus de sucre donne en général un vin plus alcoolisé. L'acide reste dans le vin et lui apporte de la fraîcheur. Les saveurs du raisin deviennent les arômes de fruits dans le verre. Le moment des vendanges oriente donc déjà le style du vin.","These changes matter because they pass straight into the wine. The sugar in the grape is what yeast will turn into alcohol, so more sugar generally means a stronger wine. The acid stays in the wine and gives it freshness. The grape's flavours become the fruit aromas in the glass. The moment of picking therefore already shapes the style of the wine."]],"k":[["Maturando l'uva si gonfia d'acqua.","En mûrissant, le raisin gonfle d'eau.","Ripening grapes swell with water."],["Lo zucchero sale, l'acido scende.","Le sucre augmente, l'acide diminue.","Sugar rises, acid falls."],["I sapori diventano più maturi.","Les saveurs deviennent plus mûres.","Flavours become riper."],["Uve bianche: da verdi a dorate; uve nere: da verdi a viola.","Raisins blancs : du vert au doré ; noirs : du vert au violet.","White grapes: green to golden; black grapes: green to purple."]]},{"c":"p1","t":["Clima fresco e clima caldo","Climat frais et climat chaud","Cool climate and warm climate"],"p":[["Le zone viticole più vicine ai poli hanno un clima fresco. Esempi tipici sono la Germania e il nord della Francia. Qui le temperature medie sono basse e il sole può essere meno forte che vicino all'Equatore; in certe annate l'uva fatica persino a maturare. Nei climi freschi è frequente coltivare uve bianche.","Les régions viticoles les plus proches des pôles ont un climat frais. L'Allemagne et le nord de la France en sont des exemples typiques. Les températures moyennes y sont basses et le soleil peut être moins fort que près de l'équateur ; certaines années, le raisin a même du mal à mûrir. Dans les climats frais, on cultive souvent des raisins blancs.","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common."],["Le zone più vicine all'Equatore hanno invece un clima caldo, come alcune parti dell'Australia e della California. Le temperature medie sono alte, il sole è più intenso e l'uva matura senza difficoltà quasi ogni anno. Nei climi caldi è frequente coltivare uve nere, che approfittano di tutto questo calore.","Les régions plus proches de l'équateur ont au contraire un climat chaud, comme certaines parties de l'Australie et de la Californie. Les températures moyennes y sont élevées, le soleil est plus intense et le raisin mûrit sans difficulté d'une année à l'autre. Dans les climats chauds, on cultive souvent des raisins noirs, qui profitent de cette chaleur.","Regions closer to the Equator have a warm climate instead, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Average temperatures are high, the sunshine is more intense and the grapes ripen reliably year after year. In warm climates it is common to grow black grapes, which make the most of all that heat."],["Il clima lascia un'impronta precisa sull'uva. In generale, più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità ci sono negli acini; più fa caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità, con sapori più maturi. Ne derivano stili diversi: un vino da clima fresco tende a essere più leggero e vivace, uno da clima caldo più ricco e maturo.","Le climat laisse une empreinte nette sur le raisin. En règle générale, plus il fait frais, moins il y a de sucre et plus il y a d'acidité dans les grains ; plus il fait chaud, plus il y a de sucre et moins d'acidité, avec des saveurs plus mûres. On obtient ainsi des styles différents : un vin de climat frais tend à être plus léger et vif, un vin de climat chaud plus riche et mûr.","Climate leaves a clear mark on the grapes. As a rule, the cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, together with riper flavours. This leads to different styles: a cool-climate wine tends to be lighter and fresher, a warm-climate wine richer and riper."],["Lo Chardonnay è un ottimo esempio. Coltivato in clima fresco dà vini con profumi di frutta verde, come la mela, e di agrumi, come il limone. Coltivato in clima caldo, lo stesso vitigno offre invece frutta a nocciolo, come la pesca, e frutta tropicale, come l'ananas. Stessa uva, stile molto diverso: è il clima a fare la differenza.","Le Chardonnay en est un bon exemple. Cultivé en climat frais, il donne des vins aux arômes de fruits verts comme la pomme et d'agrumes comme le citron. Cultivé en climat chaud, le même cépage offre plutôt des fruits à noyau comme la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas. Même raisin, style très différent : c'est le climat qui fait la différence.","Chardonnay is a good example. Grown in a cool climate, it gives wines with aromas of green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. Grown in a warm climate, the same grape shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple instead. Same grape, very different style: the climate makes the difference."]],"k":[["Clima fresco: vicino ai poli (es. Germania, nord della Francia).","Climat frais : près des pôles (ex. Allemagne, nord de la France).","Cool climate: nearer the poles (e.g. Germany, northern France)."],["Clima caldo: vicino all'Equatore (es. parti di Australia e California).","Climat chaud : près de l'équateur (ex. parties de l'Australie et de la Californie).","Warm climate: nearer the Equator (e.g. parts of Australia and California)."],["Più fresco → meno zucchero, più acidità → vino più leggero e fresco.","Plus frais → moins de sucre, plus d'acidité → vin plus léger et frais.","Cooler → less sugar, more acidity → lighter, fresher wine."],["Più caldo → più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori più maturi.","Plus chaud → plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs plus mûres.","Warmer → more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours."],["Fresco: spesso uve bianche; caldo: spesso uve nere.","Frais : souvent raisins blancs ; chaud : souvent raisins noirs.","Cool: often white grapes; warm: often black grapes."]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Tre tipi di vino: fermo, spumante, fortificato","Trois types de vin : tranquille, effervescent, fortifié","Three types of wine: still, sparkling, fortified"],"p":[["Quando qualcuno dice semplicemente «vino», di solito pensa a un vino fermo, cioè senza bollicine. È la categoria più grande. Il grado alcolico dei vini fermi va dall'8% al 15% vol., ma nella maggior parte dei casi resta tra l'11,5% e il 14%. Il valore «% vol.» (abv in inglese) indica la quota di alcol nel liquido: 10% vol. significa che un decimo del vino è alcol.","Quand on parle simplement de « vin », on pense en général à un vin tranquille, c'est-à-dire sans bulles. C'est de loin la catégorie la plus vaste. Les vins tranquilles titrent entre 8 % et 15 % vol., mais la plupart se situent entre 11,5 % et 14 %. Le chiffre « % vol. » (abv en anglais) indique la part d'alcool dans le liquide : 10 % vol. signifie qu'un dixième du vin est de l'alcool.","When people simply say «wine», they usually mean a still wine: one without bubbles. This is by far the biggest category. Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, though most sit between 11.5% and 14%. The abv figure (alcohol by volume) tells you how much of the liquid is alcohol, so a wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol."],["Molti vini fermi prendono il nome dalla zona di produzione: Sancerre e Burgundy (Bourgogne) in Francia, Rioja in Spagna, Chianti in Italia. Altri invece portano in etichetta il nome del vitigno, come un Pinot Grigio. Imparare a riconoscere queste due logiche aiuta subito a leggere le etichette e a capire che cosa aspettarsi nel bicchiere.","Beaucoup de vins tranquilles portent le nom de leur région de production : Sancerre et Burgundy (Bourgogne) en France, Rioja en Espagne, Chianti en Italie. D'autres affichent plutôt le nom du cépage, comme un Pinot Grigio. Savoir distinguer ces deux logiques aide tout de suite à lire une étiquette et à deviner ce qu'il y aura dans le verre.","Many still wines take their name from the place where they are made: Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of the grape variety instead, such as a Pinot Grigio. Spotting which of the two naming logics a label uses is a quick first step towards knowing what will be in the glass."],["I vini spumanti hanno bollicine. Durante la fermentazione si forma anidride carbonica: se il gas resta intrappolato nel vino, all'apertura della bottiglia si libera sotto forma di bollicine. Il più famoso è lo Champagne francese; molto noti anche il Cava spagnolo e il Prosecco italiano. Ma gli spumanti si producono ormai in tutto il mondo.","Les vins effervescents ont des bulles. La fermentation produit du dioxyde de carbone : si ce gaz reste piégé dans le vin, il s'échappe en bulles à l'ouverture de la bouteille. Le plus célèbre est le Champagne, en France ; le Cava espagnol et le Prosecco italien sont aussi très connus. On en produit aujourd'hui partout dans le monde.","Sparkling wines are fizzy. Fermentation creates carbon dioxide gas, and if that gas is kept trapped inside the wine, it is released as bubbles once the bottle is opened. Champagne from France is the most famous example; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also very well known. Sparkling wine is now made all around the world."],["I vini fortificati sono vini a cui è stato aggiunto altro alcol. Per questo il loro grado è più alto rispetto a quello dei vini fermi: di solito tra il 15% e il 22% vol. Due esempi classici da ricordare sono lo Sherry, dalla Spagna, e il Port (Porto), dal Portogallo. Li ritroveremo nel capitolo sugli altri vini da conoscere.","Les vins fortifiés sont des vins auxquels on a ajouté de l'alcool. Leur degré est donc plus élevé que celui des vins tranquilles : en général entre 15 % et 22 % vol. Deux exemples classiques à retenir : le Sherry (Xérès), d'Espagne, et le Port (Porto), du Portugal. Nous les retrouverons dans le chapitre consacré aux autres vins à connaître.","Fortified wines have had extra alcohol added to them. That is why they are stronger than still wines, usually somewhere between 15% and 22% abv. Two classic examples to remember are Sherry, from Spain, and Port, from Portugal. You will meet both again in the chapter on other wines to know."]],"k":[["Fermo: niente bollicine, 8–15% vol. (di solito 11,5–14%)","Tranquille : sans bulles, 8–15 % vol. (le plus souvent 11,5–14 %)","Still: no bubbles, 8–15% abv (mostly 11.5–14%)"],["Spumante: anidride carbonica della fermentazione intrappolata nel vino","Effervescent : dioxyde de carbone de la fermentation piégé dans le vin","Sparkling: carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine"],["Fortificato: alcol aggiunto, 15–22% vol. (Sherry, Port)","Fortifié : alcool ajouté, 15–22 % vol. (Sherry, Port)","Fortified: extra alcohol added, 15–22% abv (Sherry, Port)"],["Un vino può chiamarsi come la sua zona o come il suo vitigno","Un vin peut porter le nom de sa région ou de son cépage","A wine may be named after its region or its grape"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Il colore: bianco, rosso, rosato","La couleur : blanc, rouge, rosé","Colour: white, red, rosé"],"p":[["Il colore di un vino dipende da due cose: il vitigno usato e il modo in cui il vino viene fatto. Esistono uve bianche e uve nere, ma dentro si somigliano molto: la polpa ha lo stesso colore in entrambe e il succo è incolore. Il colore delle uve nere si trova tutto nella buccia, che contiene anche i tannini.","La couleur d'un vin dépend de deux choses : le cépage et la façon dont le vin est élaboré. Il existe des raisins blancs et des raisins noirs, mais à l'intérieur ils se ressemblent beaucoup : la pulpe a la même couleur et le jus est incolore. Toute la couleur des raisins noirs se trouve dans la peau, qui contient aussi les tanins.","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins."],["I vini bianchi si fanno di solito con uve bianche: pensiamo a uno Chablis o a un Riesling. Però si può ottenere un vino bianco anche da uve nere. Basta separare le bucce dal succo prima della fermentazione, per esempio con una pressatura delicata: dato che il colore è nella buccia, il succo resta chiaro e il vino sarà bianco.","Les vins blancs sont en général faits avec des raisins blancs : pensons à un Chablis ou à un Riesling. Mais on peut aussi obtenir un vin blanc à partir de raisins noirs. Il suffit de séparer les peaux du jus avant la fermentation, par exemple avec un pressurage doux : comme la couleur est dans la peau, le jus reste clair et le vin sera blanc.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white."],["Un vino rosso, invece, richiede per forza uve nere. Durante la fermentazione le bucce restano a contatto con il succo e vengono mescolate bene: così cedono colore e tannino al vino. Quando la fermentazione è finita, il vino viene separato dalle bucce. Esempi di rossi sono il Rioja spagnolo e i vini di Cabernet Sauvignon.","Un vin rouge, lui, exige des raisins noirs. Pendant la fermentation, les peaux restent au contact du jus et sont bien mélangées : elles cèdent ainsi couleur et tanins au vin. Une fois la fermentation terminée, le vin est séparé des peaux. Le Rioja espagnol et les vins de Cabernet Sauvignon sont des exemples de vins rouges.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples."],["Anche il rosato nasce da uve nere, ma il contatto con le bucce dura poco: solo qualche ora. Poi il succo, appena rosa, viene separato e termina la fermentazione senza bucce. Il risultato è un vino di colore tenue. Il White Zinfandel della California è un esempio di rosato. I rosati, inoltre, vengono affinati in legno molto raramente.","Le rosé naît lui aussi de raisins noirs, mais le contact avec les peaux est bref : seulement quelques heures. Le jus, à peine rose, est alors écoulé et termine sa fermentation sans les peaux. On obtient un vin à la couleur légère. Le White Zinfandel de Californie en est un exemple. Les rosés sont d'ailleurs rarement élevés en fût de chêne.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak."]],"k":[["Il colore delle uve nere è nella buccia; il succo è incolore","La couleur des raisins noirs est dans la peau ; le jus est incolore","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless"],["Bianco: di solito uve bianche, ma anche uve nere senza bucce","Blanc : en général raisins blancs, mais aussi raisins noirs sans les peaux","White: usually white grapes, possible from black grapes without skins"],["Rosso: solo uve nere, bucce presenti per tutta la fermentazione","Rouge : uniquement raisins noirs, peaux présentes pendant toute la fermentation","Red: black grapes only, skins kept through fermentation"],["Rosato: uve nere, poche ore di contatto con le bucce","Rosé : raisins noirs, quelques heures de contact avec les peaux","Rosé: black grapes, a few hours of skin contact"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Struttura (1): dolcezza e acidità","Structure (1) : sucrosité et acidité","Structure (1): sweetness and acidity"],"p":[["La dolcezza dipende dalla quantità di zucchero rimasta nel vino. La maggior parte dei vini è secca: per ottenerla, i lieviti devono trasformare in alcol tutto lo zucchero del succo, così nel vino ne resta pochissimo o nulla. Sono secchi, per esempio, lo Chablis e i Sauvignon Blanc tra i bianchi, il Côtes du Rhône, il Chianti e i Cabernet Sauvignon tra i rossi.","La sucrosité dépend du sucre resté dans le vin. La plupart des vins sont secs : pour cela, les levures doivent transformer en alcool tout le sucre du jus, si bien qu'il n'en reste presque pas. Sont secs, par exemple, le Chablis et les Sauvignon Blanc côté blancs, le Côtes du Rhône, le Chianti et les Cabernet Sauvignon côté rouges.","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds."],["I vini di dolcezza media sono per lo più bianchi o rosati. Si ottengono in due modi: si tolgono i lieviti prima che abbiano trasformato tutto lo zucchero, oppure si aggiunge succo d'uva non fermentato a un vino secco. Ne sono esempi alcuni Riesling tedeschi e il White Zinfandel, il rosato californiano.","Les vins de sucrosité moyenne sont surtout des blancs ou des rosés. On les obtient de deux façons : soit on retire les levures avant qu'elles aient transformé tout le sucre, soit on ajoute du jus de raisin non fermenté à un vin sec. Exemples : certains Riesling allemands et le White Zinfandel, rosé californien.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples."],["I vini dolci contengono così tanto zucchero da sembrare quasi densi e sciropposi. Possono nascere da uve talmente zuccherine che i lieviti si fermano prima di averlo consumato tutto, come nel Sauternes o in alcuni Riesling tedeschi. Nei vini fortificati, invece, si aggiunge alcol distillato ad alta gradazione che uccide i lieviti: lo zucchero rimasto rende dolci il Port e alcuni Sherry.","Les vins doux sont si riches en sucre qu'ils peuvent paraître épais, presque sirupeux. Ils peuvent venir de raisins tellement sucrés que les levures s'arrêtent avant d'avoir tout consommé, comme pour le Sauternes ou certains Riesling allemands. Dans les vins fortifiés, on ajoute un alcool distillé très fort qui tue les levures : le sucre restant rend doux le Port et certains Sherry.","Sweet wines hold so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. They can come from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before eating it all, as in Sauternes or some German Rieslings. In fortified wines, strong distilled alcohol is added, killing the yeast early; the sugar left behind makes Port and some Sherries sweet."],["L'acidità arriva direttamente dal succo d'uva ed è ciò che rende un vino rinfrescante. Si riconosce facilmente perché fa venire l'acquolina in bocca. Troppa acidità rende il vino sgradevolmente aspro; troppo poca lo rende piatto. Sono vini molto acidi lo Chablis, il Chianti e i vini di Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon e Pinot Noir.","L'acidité vient directement du jus de raisin et c'est elle qui rend un vin rafraîchissant. On la reconnaît facilement : elle fait saliver. Trop d'acidité rend le vin désagréablement acide ; trop peu, et il perd sa fraîcheur. Le Chablis, le Chianti et les vins de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon et Pinot Noir ont une acidité élevée.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity."],["Nei vini dolci l'acidità è fondamentale. Fa da contrappeso allo zucchero ed evita che il vino risulti stucchevole. Per questo un buon Sauternes o un Riesling dolce hanno sempre un'acidità alta: dolcezza e freschezza si bilanciano a vicenda e il sorso resta piacevole fino alla fine.","Dans les vins doux, l'acidité est essentielle. Elle fait contrepoids au sucre et évite que le vin devienne écœurant. C'est pourquoi un bon Sauternes ou un Riesling doux ont toujours une acidité élevée : douceur et fraîcheur s'équilibrent et la gorgée reste agréable jusqu'au bout.","In sweet wines, acidity is vital. It acts as a counterweight to the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. That is why a good Sauternes or a sweet Riesling always has high acidity: sweetness and freshness balance each other, and every sip stays enjoyable to the end."]],"k":[["Secco: i lieviti trasformano tutto lo zucchero in alcol","Sec : les levures transforment tout le sucre en alcool","Dry: yeast turn all the sugar into alcohol"],["Medio: lieviti tolti prima, o succo non fermentato aggiunto","Moyen : levures retirées tôt, ou jus non fermenté ajouté","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added"],["Dolce: uve molto zuccherine, o alcol aggiunto che uccide i lieviti","Doux : raisins très sucrés, ou alcool ajouté qui tue les levures","Sweet: very sugary grapes, or added alcohol killing the yeast"],["Acidità: viene dal succo, fa salivare, rinfresca e bilancia la dolcezza","Acidité : vient du jus, fait saliver, rafraîchit et équilibre la douceur","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Struttura (2): tannino, alcol e corpo","Structure (2) : tanins, alcool et corps","Structure (2): tannin, alcohol and body"],"p":[["Il tannino è tipico dei vini rossi e proviene dalle bucce delle uve nere. La sua quantità dipende dal vitigno e da come si fa il vino. A volte ha un gusto amaro, ma soprattutto si sente come una sensazione: lascia la bocca asciutta. Sono ricchi di tannino il Bordeaux rosso e il Chianti; ne hanno poco il Beaujolais e alcuni Pinot Noir.","Le tanin est propre aux vins rouges et vient de la peau des raisins noirs. Sa quantité dépend du cépage et de la vinification. Il peut paraître amer, mais on le perçoit surtout comme une sensation : il assèche la bouche. Le Bordeaux rouge et le Chianti sont riches en tanins ; le Beaujolais et certains Pinot Noir en ont peu.","Tannin belongs to red wines and comes from the skins of black grapes. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on the winemaking. It can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel: it leaves your mouth dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin; Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low."],["Quasi tutti i vini fermi e spumanti hanno tra l'11,5% e il 14% vol. Alcuni arrivano fino al 15%, altri scendono fino all'8%. Un esempio di vino molto alcolico è lo Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rosso francese; un esempio di vino poco alcolico è il White Zinfandel californiano. Ricorda: l'alcol nasce dalla fermentazione dello zucchero.","Presque tous les vins tranquilles et effervescents titrent entre 11,5 % et 14 % vol. Certains montent jusqu'à 15 %, d'autres descendent jusqu'à 8 %. Le Châteauneuf-du-Pape, rouge français, est un exemple de vin riche en alcool ; le White Zinfandel californien, un exemple de vin peu alcoolisé. Rappel : l'alcool naît de la fermentation du sucre.","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar."],["Il corpo descrive la sensazione generale del vino in bocca. Molti fattori lo influenzano, quindi la domanda più semplice è: quanto riempie la bocca? Un vino di corpo pieno sembra denso e avvolgente, uno leggero più delicato. Leggeri: Pinot Grigio e Beaujolais. Medi: Sancerre e Côtes du Rhône. Pieni: Cabernet Sauvignon della California e Sauternes.","Le corps décrit la sensation globale du vin en bouche. Beaucoup de facteurs y contribuent, alors la question la plus simple est : à quel point remplit-il la bouche ? Un vin corsé paraît dense et enveloppant, un vin léger plus délicat. Légers : Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Moyens : Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Corsés : Cabernet Sauvignon de Californie, Sauternes.","Body describes the overall feel of a wine in your mouth. Many things contribute to it, so the easiest question to ask is: how mouth-filling is it? Full-bodied wines feel dense and rich, while light-bodied ones feel more delicate. Light: Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Medium: Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Full: Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauternes."]],"k":[["Tannino: dalle bucce, asciuga la bocca, tipico dei rossi","Tanin : vient des peaux, assèche la bouche, typique des rouges","Tannin: from skins, dries the mouth, a red-wine feature"],["Alcol: di solito 11,5–14% vol., tra 8% e 15% per vini fermi e spumanti","Alcool : en général 11,5–14 % vol., entre 8 et 15 % pour tranquilles et effervescents","Alcohol: usually 11.5–14% abv, 8–15% for still and sparkling"],["Corpo: quanto il vino riempie la bocca (leggero, medio, pieno)","Corps : à quel point le vin remplit la bouche (léger, moyen, corsé)","Body: how mouth-filling the wine is (light, medium, full)"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Aromi e sapori: frutta, legno, altro","Arômes et saveurs : fruit, bois, autres","Aromas and flavours: fruit, oak, other"],"p":[["Gli aromi e i sapori di un vino hanno origini diverse. Alcuni arrivano direttamente dalle uve, altri si sviluppano durante la vinificazione e l'affinamento. All'inizio descriverli può sembrare difficile, ma è un'abilità che migliora con la pratica. Un metodo semplice è chiedersi: sento frutta? Sento legno? Sento qualcos'altro?","Les arômes et saveurs d'un vin ont des origines variées. Certains viennent directement du raisin, d'autres apparaissent pendant la vinification et l'élevage. Les décrire peut sembler difficile au début, mais cela s'apprend avec la pratique. Une méthode simple : se demander si l'on sent du fruit, du bois ou autre chose.","A wine's aromas and flavours come from different places. Some come straight from the grapes, while others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words feels hard at first, but it is a skill that grows with practice. A simple method is to ask three questions: do I notice fruit? Oak? Something else?"],["Quasi tutti i vini profumano di frutta. Il tipo di frutta dipende prima di tutto dal vitigno: il Cabernet Sauvignon, per esempio, sa di ribes nero. Conta anche la maturità delle uve: uno Chardonnay di clima fresco ricorda la mela verde e il limone, mentre uno di clima caldo ricorda la pesca e frutti tropicali come l'ananas.","Presque tous les vins sentent le fruit. Le type de fruit dépend d'abord du cépage : le Cabernet Sauvignon, par exemple, évoque le cassis. La maturité du raisin compte aussi : un Chardonnay de climat frais rappelle la pomme verte et le citron, tandis qu'un Chardonnay de climat chaud évoque la pêche et des fruits tropicaux comme l'ananas.","Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends first on the grape variety: Cabernet Sauvignon, for instance, smells of blackcurrant. Ripeness matters too. A Chardonnay from a cool climate shows green apple and lemon, whereas one from a warm climate leans towards peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple."],["Il vino può fermentare e/o affinarsi in botti di rovere. In quel caso il legno aggiunge note come vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro e affumicato. A volte l'uso del legno è indicato in etichetta. Quando senti questi profumi accanto alla frutta, è un buon indizio che il vino sia passato in botte.","Le vin peut fermenter et/ou être élevé en fût de chêne. Le bois apporte alors des notes de vanille, de noix de coco, de clou de girofle, de cèdre ou de fumé. L'usage du chêne est parfois indiqué sur l'étiquette. Quand on perçoit ces arômes à côté du fruit, c'est un bon indice d'un passage en fût.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel."],["Infine ci sono gli «altri» aromi, che rendono il vino così vario e interessante: erba, fiori, erbe aromatiche, ortaggi, terra, funghi, cuoio. Per esempio, un Sauvignon Blanc può far pensare all'erba appena tagliata, mentre il Chianti può avere note di erbe secche. Raggrupparli in una famiglia a parte aiuta a non confonderli con la frutta.","Restent les « autres » arômes, qui rendent le vin si varié et passionnant : herbe, fleurs, herbes aromatiques, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir. Un Sauvignon Blanc peut par exemple évoquer l'herbe coupée, et le Chianti des herbes séchées. Les ranger dans une famille à part évite de les confondre avec le fruit.","Finally, there are the «other» aromas that make wine so varied and interesting: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. A Sauvignon Blanc, for example, can bring cut grass to mind, while Chianti can show dried herbs. Keeping them in a family of their own stops you confusing them with fruit."]],"k":[["Frutta: dipende dal vitigno e dalla maturità delle uve","Fruit : dépend du cépage et de la maturité du raisin","Fruit: depends on the grape variety and its ripeness"],["Clima fresco = mela, limone; clima caldo = pesca, ananas","Climat frais = pomme, citron ; climat chaud = pêche, ananas","Cool climate = apple, lemon; warm climate = peach, pineapple"],["Legno di rovere: vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, affumicato","Chêne : vanille, noix de coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumé","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke"],["Altro: erba, fiori, erbe, ortaggi, terra, funghi, cuoio","Autres : herbe, fleurs, herbes, légumes, terre, champignon, cuir","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather"]]},{"c":"w1","t":["Lo stile: la somma delle caratteristiche","Le style : la somme des caractéristiques","Style: the sum of the characteristics"],"p":[["Ognuno dei tre tipi di vino, fermo, spumante o fortificato, può presentarsi in tanti stili diversi. Lo stile è l'insieme di tre elementi: il colore, la struttura (dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol, corpo) e gli aromi e sapori. Descrivere uno stile significa mettere insieme questi pezzi in un ritratto unico del vino.","Chacun des trois types de vin, tranquille, effervescent ou fortifié, peut se décliner en de nombreux styles. Le style réunit trois éléments : la couleur, la structure (sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool, corps) et les arômes et saveurs. Décrire un style, c'est assembler ces pièces pour dresser le portrait complet d'un vin.","Each of the three types of wine, still, sparkling or fortified, can come in many different styles. A style brings together three elements: colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. Describing a style means putting these pieces together into one complete portrait of the wine."],["Un confronto lo rende chiaro. Lo Chablis e il Sauternes sono entrambi bianchi francesi, eppure hanno stili opposti. Lo Chablis è secco, molto acido, di corpo leggero o medio, con mela verde e limone e senza legno. Il Sauternes è dolce, di corpo pieno, con albicocca, miele e vaniglia del rovere, sostenuto da un'acidità alta.","Une comparaison rend l'idée claire. Le Chablis et le Sauternes sont tous deux des blancs français, et pourtant leurs styles s'opposent. Le Chablis est sec, très acide, léger à moyen en corps, avec pomme verte et citron, sans bois. Le Sauternes est doux, corsé, avec abricot, miel et vanille du chêne, porté par une acidité élevée.","A comparison makes this clear. Chablis and Sauternes are both French white wines, yet their styles are opposites. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium in body, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity."],["Lo stile dipende molto dal clima in cui crescono le uve. Più fa fresco, meno zucchero e più acidità hanno le uve: ne nascono vini più freschi e leggeri, con frutta verde e agrumi. Più fa caldo, più zucchero e meno acidità: i sapori sono più maturi e, dato che lo zucchero diventa alcol, i vini tendono a essere più alcolici e corposi.","Le style dépend beaucoup du climat où pousse le raisin. Plus il fait frais, moins le raisin a de sucre et plus il a d'acidité : on obtient des vins plus frais et légers, aux fruits verts et agrumes. Plus il fait chaud, plus il y a de sucre et moins d'acidité : les saveurs sont plus mûres et, le sucre devenant alcool, les vins sont plus alcoolisés et plus amples.","Style depends a lot on the climate where the grapes grow. The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have, giving fresher, lighter wines with green fruit and citrus. The warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity: flavours taste riper and, since sugar becomes alcohol, wines tend to be stronger and fuller."],["Per descrivere uno stile si segue un approccio sistematico alla degustazione. Prima l'aspetto: il colore (bianco, rosso, rosato). Poi il naso: aromi di frutta, legno o altro. Infine il palato: dolcezza, acidità, tannino, alcol e corpo, più i sapori. Usare sempre lo stesso ordine aiuta chi studia a confrontare i vini e a ricordarli.","Pour décrire un style, on suit une approche systématique de la dégustation. D'abord l'aspect : la couleur (blanc, rouge, rosé). Puis le nez : arômes de fruit, de bois ou autres. Enfin la bouche : sucrosité, acidité, tanins, alcool et corps, plus les saveurs. Suivre toujours le même ordre aide les personnes qui étudient à comparer les vins et à s'en souvenir.","To describe a style, you follow a systematic approach to tasting. First the appearance: the colour (white, red, rosé). Then the nose: aromas of fruit, oak or other. Finally the palate: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, plus the flavours. Always using the same order makes it easier to compare wines and remember them."]],"k":[["Stile = colore + struttura + aromi e sapori","Style = couleur + structure + arômes et saveurs","Style = colour + structure + aromas and flavours"],["Clima fresco: più acidità, meno zucchero, vini più leggeri e freschi","Climat frais : plus d'acidité, moins de sucre, vins plus légers et frais","Cool climate: more acid, less sugar, lighter and fresher wines"],["Clima caldo: più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori più maturi","Climat chaud : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs plus mûres","Warm climate: more sugar, less acid, riper flavours"],["Degustazione: aspetto, naso, palato, sempre nello stesso ordine","Dégustation : aspect, nez, bouche, toujours dans le même ordre","Tasting: appearance, nose, palate, always in the same order"]]}],"flash":[{"c":"p1","f":["Buccia dell'uva nera","Peau du raisin noir","Black grape skin"],"b":["Colore intenso e tannini, che lasciano la bocca secca.","Couleur intense et tanins, qui assèchent la bouche.","Deep colour and tannins, which make the mouth feel dry."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Polpa dell'uva","Pulpe du raisin","Grape pulp"],"b":["Parte morbida con il succo: acqua, zucchero e acido. Stesso colore in tutte le uve.","Partie tendre contenant le jus : eau, sucre et acide. Même couleur dans tous les raisins.","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Tannini","Tanins","Tannins"],"b":["Sostanze della buccia delle uve nere che asciugano la bocca.","Substances de la peau des raisins noirs qui assèchent la bouche.","Substances in black grape skins that dry out the mouth."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Ciclo annuale della vite","Cycle annuel de la vigne","The vine's yearly cycle"],"b":["Fioritura in primavera, maturazione in estate, vendemmia a fine estate.","Floraison au printemps, maturation en été, vendanges en fin d'été.","Flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking in late summer."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Che cosa cambia quando l'uva matura?","Que change-t-il quand le raisin mûrit ?","What changes as grapes ripen?"],"b":["Più acqua e zucchero, meno acido, sapori più maturi, cambio di colore.","Plus d'eau et de sucre, moins d'acide, saveurs plus mûres, changement de couleur.","More water and sugar, less acid, riper flavours, colour change."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Clima fresco","Climat frais","Cool climate"],"b":["Vicino ai poli (Germania, nord della Francia): meno zucchero, più acidità; spesso uve bianche.","Près des pôles (Allemagne, nord de la France) : moins de sucre, plus d'acidité ; souvent raisins blancs.","Nearer the poles (Germany, northern France): less sugar, more acidity; often white grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Clima caldo","Climat chaud","Warm climate"],"b":["Vicino all'Equatore (parti di Australia e California): più zucchero, meno acidità, sapori maturi; spesso uve nere.","Près de l'équateur (parties de l'Australie et de la Californie) : plus de sucre, moins d'acidité, saveurs mûres ; souvent raisins noirs.","Nearer the Equator (parts of Australia and California): more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours; often black grapes."]},{"c":"p1","f":["Chardonnay: clima fresco o caldo?","Chardonnay : climat frais ou chaud ?","Chardonnay: cool or warm climate?"],"b":["Fresco: mela e limone. Caldo: pesca e ananas.","Frais : pomme et citron. Chaud : pêche et ananas.","Cool: apple and lemon. Warm: peach and pineapple."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino fermo","Vin tranquille","Still wine"],"b":["Vino senza bollicine; 8–15% vol., di solito 11,5–14%.","Vin sans bulles ; 8–15 % vol., le plus souvent 11,5–14 %.","Wine without bubbles; 8–15% abv, mostly 11.5–14%."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino spumante","Vin effervescent","Sparkling wine"],"b":["Bollicine di anidride carbonica della fermentazione. Es.: Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Bulles de dioxyde de carbone issu de la fermentation. Ex. : Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Bubbles of carbon dioxide from fermentation. E.g. Champagne, Cava, Prosecco."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino fortificato","Vin fortifié","Fortified wine"],"b":["Vino con alcol aggiunto, 15–22% vol. Es.: Sherry, Port.","Vin additionné d'alcool, 15–22 % vol. Ex. : Sherry, Port.","Wine with added alcohol, 15–22% abv. E.g. Sherry, Port."]},{"c":"w1","f":["% vol. (abv)","% vol. (abv)","abv"],"b":["Percentuale di alcol nel volume: 10% = un decimo del vino è alcol.","Part d'alcool dans le volume : 10 % = un dixième du vin est de l'alcool.","Alcohol by volume: 10% means one tenth of the liquid is alcohol."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino secco","Vin sec","Dry wine"],"b":["Zucchero assente o minimo: i lieviti l'hanno trasformato tutto in alcol.","Pas ou très peu de sucre : les levures l'ont tout transformé en alcool.","No or very little sugar: the yeast turned it all into alcohol."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Acidità","Acidité","Acidity"],"b":["Viene dal succo d'uva, fa salivare, rinfresca e bilancia la dolcezza.","Vient du jus de raisin, fait saliver, rafraîchit et équilibre la douceur.","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Tannino","Tanin","Tannin"],"b":["Dalle bucce delle uve nere; asciuga la bocca. Alto: Bordeaux rosso, Chianti.","Vient de la peau des raisins noirs ; assèche la bouche. Élevé : Bordeaux rouge, Chianti.","From black grape skins; dries the mouth. High: red Bordeaux, Chianti."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Corpo","Corps","Body"],"b":["Quanto il vino riempie la bocca: leggero (Pinot Grigio), medio (Sancerre), pieno (Sauternes).","À quel point le vin remplit la bouche : léger (Pinot Grigio), moyen (Sancerre), corsé (Sauternes).","How mouth-filling a wine is: light (Pinot Grigio), medium (Sancerre), full (Sauternes)."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Aromi del rovere","Arômes du chêne","Oak aromas"],"b":["Vaniglia, cocco, chiodi di garofano, cedro, affumicato.","Vanille, noix de coco, clou de girofle, cèdre, fumé.","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke."]},{"c":"w1","f":["Vino rosato","Vin rosé","Rosé wine"],"b":["Uve nere, poche ore di contatto con le bucce, poi fermentazione senza bucce.","Raisins noirs, quelques heures avec les peaux, puis fermentation sans elles.","Black grapes, a few hours on the skins, then fermented without them."]}]};
window.TWG_ESX={"es":{"Inside a grape":"Cómo es una uva por dentro","Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine.":"El vino parte de una idea sencilla: se estrujan las uvas para liberar su zumo dulce y después se deja fermentar. Por eso el vino se puede definir como zumo de uva fermentado. Para entender lo que acabará en la copa, conviene empezar por la uva, que tiene dos partes principales: la piel por fuera y la pulpa por dentro. Cada una aporta algo distinto al vino.","There are two broad families of grapes: white and black. Cut in half, they look very much alike, because the real difference lies mainly in the skin. Black grapes have deeply coloured skins that also hold tannins, substances that leave your mouth feeling dry. White grapes, once ripe, have skins with a golden colour.":"Hay dos grandes familias de uvas: blancas y tintas. Cortadas por la mitad se parecen mucho, porque la diferencia está sobre todo en la piel. Las uvas tintas tienen una piel de color intenso que además contiene taninos, unas sustancias que dejan la boca con sensación de sequedad. Las uvas blancas, cuando están maduras, tienen la piel de color dorado.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda y carnosa de la uva y es la que contiene el zumo. Ese zumo está formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Un detalle importante: la pulpa tiene el mismo color tanto en las uvas blancas como en las tintas. Por eso el color de un vino tinto no viene del zumo sino de las pieles, una idea clave para entender después cómo se elaboran los distintos vinos.","Wine is fermented grape juice.":"El vino es zumo de uva fermentado.","Black grape skins: deep colour and tannins.":"Piel de las uvas tintas: color intenso y taninos.","Tannins make the mouth feel dry.":"Los taninos dejan la boca seca.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid.":"Pulpa: zumo de agua, azúcar y ácido.","Pulp is the same colour in white and black grapes.":"La pulpa tiene el mismo color en uvas blancas y tintas.","The vine's year":"El año de la vid","Grapes are the fruit of the grape vine, a plant that can live for several decades. After planting, a vine needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year. Its cycle follows the seasons: it flowers in spring, the fruit ripens through the summer and the grapes are picked towards the end of summer.":"La uva es el fruto de la vid, una planta que puede vivir varias décadas. Tras plantarla, la vid necesita un par de años para llegar a la madurez; a partir de entonces da una cosecha cada año. Su ciclo sigue las estaciones: florece en primavera, el fruto madura durante el verano y la vendimia llega hacia el final del verano.","In spring the vine produces clusters of tiny flowers. Each single flower is set to become one grape. Right after flowering, the young grapes are small, hard and green, whether they will end up white or black: at this stage you cannot yet tell them apart, and they are far from ready to make wine.":"En primavera la vid produce racimos de flores diminutas. Cada flor está destinada a convertirse en una uva. Justo después de la floración, las uvas recién formadas son pequeñas, duras y verdes, tanto si serán blancas como tintas: en esta fase todavía no se distinguen y están lejos de servir para hacer vino.","To grow well and give good quality fruit, a vine needs the right amount of sunlight and heat: if it is too cold or too hot, it cannot manage. Vines also do best where the winter is cold enough to let them rest. That is why most vineyards lie in two bands around the globe, roughly between 30° and 50° of latitude, north and south of the Equator.":"Para crecer bien y dar uva de calidad, la vid necesita la cantidad justa de sol y de calor: si hace demasiado frío o demasiado calor, no lo consigue. Además, prefiere zonas donde el invierno sea lo bastante frío para que pueda descansar. Por eso la mayoría de los viñedos están en dos franjas del planeta, más o menos entre los 30° y los 50° de latitud, al norte y al sur del ecuador.","A mature vine gives a crop every year and can live for decades.":"Una vid adulta da una cosecha al año y puede vivir décadas.","Spring: flowering; each flower becomes a grape.":"Primavera: floración; cada flor se convierte en una uva.","Summer: ripening; late summer: harvest.":"Verano: maduración; final del verano: vendimia.","Vines need the right sun and heat, plus a cold winter to rest.":"La vid necesita sol y calor justos y un invierno frío para descansar.","What happens as grapes ripen":"Qué ocurre cuando la uva madura","Over the summer the small, hard grapes change a great deal. They swell as they fill with water, while their sugar content goes up and their acid content goes down. Their flavours also develop and become riper. An unripe grape is therefore sour and not very tasty, whereas a ripe grape is bigger, sweeter and less acidic.":"Durante el verano, las uvas pequeñas y duras cambian mucho. Se hinchan al llenarse de agua y, al mismo tiempo, su contenido de azúcar sube y el de ácido baja. Los sabores también evolucionan y se vuelven más maduros. Una uva verde es, por tanto, agria y poco sabrosa, mientras que una uva madura es más grande, más dulce y menos ácida.","Ripening also changes the colour of the skin. White grapes turn from green to golden, while black grapes turn from green to purple. Colour is therefore a first clue to how close the grapes are to harvest, alongside the other changes: more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"Con la maduración también cambia el color de la piel. Las uvas blancas pasan del verde a un tono dorado, y las uvas tintas pasan del verde al morado. El color es, por tanto, una primera pista de lo cerca que está la vendimia, junto con los demás cambios: más agua, más azúcar, menos ácido y sabores más maduros.","These changes matter because they pass straight into the wine. The sugar in the grape is what yeast will turn into alcohol, so more sugar generally means a stronger wine. The acid stays in the wine and gives it freshness. The grape's flavours become the fruit aromas in the glass. The moment of picking therefore already shapes the style of the wine.":"Estos cambios importan porque pasan directamente al vino. El azúcar de la uva es lo que las levaduras convertirán en alcohol, así que más azúcar suele significar un vino con más alcohol. El ácido se queda en el vino y le da frescura. Los sabores de la uva se convierten en los aromas de fruta de la copa. El momento de la vendimia ya orienta, por tanto, el estilo del vino.","Ripening grapes swell with water.":"Al madurar, la uva se hincha de agua.","Sugar rises, acid falls.":"El azúcar sube y el ácido baja.","Flavours become riper.":"Los sabores se vuelven más maduros.","White grapes: green to golden; black grapes: green to purple.":"Uvas blancas: de verde a dorado; tintas: de verde a morado.","Cool climate and warm climate":"Clima fresco y clima cálido","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common.":"Las regiones vitícolas más cercanas a los polos tienen un clima fresco. Alemania y el norte de Francia son ejemplos típicos. Allí las temperaturas medias son bajas y el sol puede ser más débil que cerca del ecuador; algunos años a la uva incluso le cuesta madurar. En los climas frescos es habitual cultivar uvas blancas.","Regions closer to the Equator have a warm climate instead, such as parts of Australia and parts of California. Average temperatures are high, the sunshine is more intense and the grapes ripen reliably year after year. In warm climates it is common to grow black grapes, which make the most of all that heat.":"Las regiones más cercanas al ecuador tienen, en cambio, un clima cálido, como algunas partes de Australia y de California. Las temperaturas medias son altas, el sol es más intenso y la uva madura sin problemas año tras año. En los climas cálidos es habitual cultivar uvas tintas, que aprovechan todo ese calor.","Climate leaves a clear mark on the grapes. As a rule, the cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, together with riper flavours. This leads to different styles: a cool-climate wine tends to be lighter and fresher, a warm-climate wine richer and riper.":"El clima deja una huella clara en la uva. Por regla general, cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tienen las uvas; cuanto más calor, más azúcar y menos acidez, con sabores más maduros. De ahí salen estilos distintos: un vino de clima fresco tiende a ser más ligero y vivo, y uno de clima cálido, más rico y maduro.","Chardonnay is a good example. Grown in a cool climate, it gives wines with aromas of green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. Grown in a warm climate, the same grape shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple instead. Same grape, very different style: the climate makes the difference.":"La Chardonnay es un buen ejemplo. Cultivada en clima fresco, da vinos con aromas de fruta verde, como la manzana, y de cítricos, como el limón. Cultivada en clima cálido, la misma uva ofrece en cambio fruta de hueso, como el melocotón, y fruta tropical, como la piña. Misma uva, estilo muy distinto: el clima marca la diferencia.","Cool climate: nearer the poles (e.g. Germany, northern France).":"Clima fresco: cerca de los polos (p. ej. Alemania, norte de Francia).","Warm climate: nearer the Equator (e.g. parts of Australia and California).":"Clima cálido: cerca del ecuador (p. ej. partes de Australia y California).","Cooler → less sugar, more acidity → lighter, fresher wine.":"Más fresco → menos azúcar, más acidez → vino más ligero y fresco.","Warmer → more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours.":"Más cálido → más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores más maduros.","Cool: often white grapes; warm: often black grapes.":"Fresco: a menudo uvas blancas; cálido: a menudo uvas tintas.","Which definition best describes wine?":"¿Qué definición describe mejor el vino?","Fermented grape juice":"Zumo de uva fermentado","Distilled grape juice":"Zumo de uva destilado","Concentrated grape juice":"Zumo de uva concentrado","Pasteurised grape juice":"Zumo de uva pasteurizado","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes.":"El vino se obtiene haciendo fermentar el zumo dulce de la uva.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine.":"Para hacer vino se estrujan las uvas y se libera su zumo dulce. Después, la fermentación alcohólica, gracias a las levaduras, convierte el azúcar de ese zumo en alcohol. Sin fermentación solo quedaría zumo de uva; destilar o concentrar el zumo no forma parte de la definición básica del vino.","Which part of a black grape contains tannins?":"¿En qué parte de la uva tinta se encuentran los taninos?","The skin":"En la piel","The pulp":"En la pulpa","The juice":"En el zumo","The flower":"En la flor","Black grape skins hold both the colour and the tannins.":"La piel de las uvas tintas contiene tanto el color como los taninos.","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes.":"La piel es lo que distingue de verdad las uvas tintas de las blancas: tiene un color intenso y contiene taninos, que dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca. La pulpa, en cambio, contiene el zumo, formado por agua, azúcar y ácido, y tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas.","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?":"¿De qué está compuesto principalmente el zumo de la pulpa?","Water, sugar and acid":"Agua, azúcar y ácido","Water, tannin and colour":"Agua, taninos y color","Alcohol, sugar and yeast":"Alcohol, azúcar y levadura","Water, alcohol and carbon dioxide":"Agua, alcohol y dióxido de carbono","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid.":"El zumo de uva es sobre todo agua, azúcar y ácido.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda de la uva y contiene el zumo, formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Los taninos y el color están en la piel. El alcohol y el dióxido de carbono solo aparecen más tarde, cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar del zumo.","What do tannins do to your mouth?":"¿Qué sensación dejan los taninos en la boca?","Make it feel dry":"La dejan seca","Make it water":"La hacen salivar","Make it feel hot":"La calientan","Make it feel sweet":"La endulzan","Tannins from the skins leave the mouth feeling dry.":"Los taninos de la piel dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca.","Tannins come from black grape skins and are felt more than tasted: they dry out the mouth. When tasting, they should not be confused with acidity, which makes your mouth water instead, or with alcohol, which gives a warming sensation.":"Los taninos proceden de la piel de las uvas tintas y se notan más como una sensación que como un sabor: secan la boca. No hay que confundirlos con la acidez, que hace salivar, ni con el alcohol, que da sensación de calor.","What colour is the pulp of a black grape?":"¿De qué color es la pulpa de una uva tinta?","The same as in a white grape":"El mismo que en una uva blanca","Deep red, like the skin":"Rojo intenso, como la piel","Purple, but only when fully ripe":"Morada, pero solo cuando está madura","Pink, paler than the skin":"Rosa, más clara que la piel","Pulp is the same colour in all grapes; the colour is in the skin.":"La pulpa tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas; el color está en la piel.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away.":"Por dentro, las uvas blancas y tintas se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color sea cual sea el de la piel. Precisamente por eso el color de un vino tinto viene de las pieles, y por eso se puede hacer incluso un vino blanco con uvas tintas si se separa el zumo de las pieles enseguida.","In which season does the grape vine flower?":"¿En qué estación florece la vid?","Spring":"En primavera","Summer":"En verano","Autumn":"En otoño","Winter":"En invierno","Vines flower in spring; the grapes then ripen in summer.":"La vid florece en primavera; luego la uva madura en verano.","The vine's yearly cycle follows the seasons. In spring the clusters of flowers appear, and each flower will become a grape. During summer the grapes ripen, and they are picked towards the end of summer. In winter the vine rests, and it needs enough cold to do so.":"El ciclo anual de la vid sigue las estaciones. En primavera aparecen los racimos de flores, y cada flor se convertirá en una uva. En verano la uva madura y hacia el final del verano se vendimia. En invierno, en cambio, la vid descansa, y necesita suficiente frío para hacerlo.","What does each individual vine flower become?":"¿En qué se convierte cada flor de la vid?","One grape":"Una uva","A new shoot":"Un nuevo brote","A whole leaf":"Una hoja entera","A whole bunch":"Un racimo entero","After flowering, each single flower turns into a small grape.":"Tras la floración, cada flor se transforma en una uva pequeña.","Vine flowers come in clusters made up of many tiny flowers. After flowering, each one becomes a grape, so the cluster of flowers turns into a bunch of grapes. At first these grapes are small, hard and green; they only grow and ripen as the summer goes on.":"Las flores de la vid forman racimos compuestos por muchas flores diminutas. Tras la floración, cada una se convierte en una uva, así que el racimo de flores se transforma en un racimo de uvas. Al principio son pequeñas, duras y verdes; solo crecen y maduran a lo largo del verano.","What are grapes like just after flowering?":"¿Cómo son las uvas justo después de la floración?","Small, hard and green":"Pequeñas, duras y verdes","Small, soft and golden":"Pequeñas, blandas y doradas","Large, hard and purple":"Grandes, duras y moradas","Large, soft and sweet":"Grandes, blandas y dulces","All young grapes are small, hard and green, white or black.":"Todas las uvas jóvenes son pequeñas, duras y verdes, blancas o tintas.","Newly formed grapes are not ready yet: they are small, hard and green, and at this stage white and black grapes look the same. Only during summer ripening do they swell with water, become sweeter and change colour, towards golden for white grapes and purple for black ones.":"Recién formadas, las uvas aún no están listas: son pequeñas, duras y verdes, y en esta fase no se distinguen las blancas de las tintas. Solo con la maduración del verano se hinchan de agua, se vuelven más dulces y cambian de color, hacia el dorado las blancas y hacia el morado las tintas.","As grapes ripen, what happens to their sugar and acid levels?":"Durante la maduración, ¿qué ocurre con los niveles de azúcar y de ácido de la uva?","Sugar rises and acid falls":"El azúcar sube y el ácido baja","Sugar falls and acid rises":"El azúcar baja y el ácido sube","Both rise at the same rate":"Ambos suben al mismo ritmo","Both stay the same":"Ambos se mantienen igual","Ripening makes grapes sweeter and less acidic.":"Al madurar, la uva se vuelve más dulce y menos ácida.","While grapes ripen over the summer, several things change: they swell with water, sugar goes up, acid goes down and the flavours become riper. This balance between sugar and acid will later influence the alcohol and freshness of the wine.":"Mientras la uva madura en verano se producen varios cambios: las uvas se hinchan de agua, el azúcar aumenta, el ácido disminuye y los sabores se vuelven más maduros. Este equilibrio entre azúcar y ácido influirá más tarde en el alcohol y la frescura del vino.","What colour do white grapes turn as they ripen?":"¿De qué color se vuelven las uvas blancas al madurar?","From green to golden":"De verde a dorado","From green to purple":"De verde a morado","From yellow to green":"De amarillo a verde","From golden to pink":"De dorado a rosa","White grapes go from green to golden; black ones from green to purple.":"Las uvas blancas pasan de verde a dorado; las tintas, de verde a morado.","At first all grapes are green. As they ripen, the skin changes colour: it becomes golden in white grapes and purple in black grapes. This colour change goes hand in hand with the other signs of ripening, namely more water, more sugar, less acid and riper flavours.":"Al principio todas las uvas son verdes. Con la maduración, la piel cambia de color: se vuelve dorada en las uvas blancas y morada en las tintas. Este cambio acompaña a las demás señales de maduración: más agua, más azúcar, menos ácido y sabores más maduros.","Which of these does NOT happen as grapes ripen?":"¿Cuál de estos cambios NO ocurre cuando la uva madura?","Acidity increases":"La acidez aumenta","Grapes swell with water":"Las uvas se hinchan de agua","Sugar increases":"El azúcar aumenta","Flavours become riper":"Los sabores maduran","During ripening acidity falls, it does not rise.":"Durante la maduración la acidez baja, no sube.","Ripening brings more water into the grapes, more sugar and riper flavours, but acid moves the other way and drops. That is why an unripe grape tastes sour, while a ripe one is sweet and less acidic. Remembering this trend also helps you understand the effect of climate.":"La maduración aporta más agua a las uvas, más azúcar y sabores más maduros, pero el ácido va en sentido contrario y disminuye. Por eso una uva verde es agria y una madura es dulce y menos ácida. Recordar esta tendencia ayuda también a entender el efecto del clima.","In the vine's yearly cycle, when are the grapes usually picked?":"Según el ciclo de la vid, ¿cuándo se suele vendimiar?","In late summer":"A finales del verano","In early spring":"A principios de primavera","In midwinter":"En pleno invierno","Just after flowering":"Justo después de la floración","Grapes ripen through summer and are picked in late summer.":"La uva madura en verano y se recoge hacia el final del verano.","The vine flowers in spring, the flowers become grapes and these ripen during the summer. Once they are ripe enough, towards the end of summer, they are picked. Just after flowering the grapes are still small, hard and green, far too unripe to make wine.":"La vid florece en primavera, las flores se convierten en uvas y estas maduran durante el verano. Cuando están lo bastante maduras, hacia el final del verano, se recogen. Justo después de la floración las uvas son todavía pequeñas, duras y verdes, demasiado verdes para hacer vino.","Why do vines grow best where winters are cold?":"¿Por qué la vid crece mejor donde el invierno es frío?","The cold lets the vine rest":"Porque el frío le permite descansar","The cold raises sugar levels":"Porque el frío aumenta el azúcar","The cold makes the vine flower":"Porque el frío hace florecer la vid","The cold colours the skins":"Porque el frío colorea las pieles","A cold enough winter gives the vine a period of rest.":"Un invierno lo bastante frío da a la vid un periodo de descanso.","Besides the right amount of sunlight and heat during the growing season, a vine needs a winter cold enough to let it rest. This is why most vineyards are found in particular bands of latitude, neither too cold nor too hot.":"Además de la cantidad justa de sol y calor durante la temporada de crecimiento, la vid necesita un invierno lo bastante frío para poder descansar. Por eso la mayoría de los viñedos se encuentra en franjas de latitud concretas, ni demasiado frías ni demasiado cálidas.","Which of these is an example of a cool climate wine region?":"¿Cuál de estos es un ejemplo de región vitícola de clima fresco?","Germany":"Alemania","Parts of Australia":"Algunas zonas de Australia","Parts of California":"Algunas zonas de California","Areas on the Equator":"Las zonas del ecuador","Germany, like northern France, lies nearer the poles and has a cool climate.":"Alemania, como el norte de Francia, está más cerca de los polos y tiene clima fresco.","Cool climate regions are those closer to the poles, such as Germany and northern France. Parts of Australia and California are examples of warm climates instead. Right at the Equator it is too hot for vines to grow well and rest in winter.":"Las regiones de clima fresco son las más cercanas a los polos, como Alemania y el norte de Francia. Algunas partes de Australia y de California son, en cambio, ejemplos de clima cálido. Junto al ecuador hace demasiado calor para que la vid crezca bien y descanse en invierno.","Which type of grape is commonly grown in warm climate regions?":"¿Qué tipo de uva se cultiva con más frecuencia en las regiones cálidas?","Black grapes":"Las uvas tintas","White grapes":"Las uvas blancas","Unripe grapes":"Las uvas verdes","Skinless grapes":"Las uvas sin piel","Warm climates ripen grapes reliably, and black grapes are commonly grown.":"En clima cálido la uva madura con regularidad y es habitual cultivar uvas tintas.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown.":"Las regiones cálidas, más cercanas al ecuador, tienen temperaturas medias altas y un sol más intenso, así que la uva madura con regularidad. Allí es habitual cultivar uvas tintas. En las regiones frescas, donde a veces a la uva le cuesta madurar, es más frecuente cultivar uvas blancas.","In a cool climate, grapes will usually have…":"En un clima fresco, ¿cómo suelen ser las uvas?","Less sugar and more acidity":"Menos azúcar y más acidez","More sugar and less acidity":"Más azúcar y menos acidez","More sugar and more acidity":"Más azúcar y más acidez","Less sugar and less acidity":"Menos azúcar y menos acidez","The cooler it is, the more acidic and less sugary the grapes stay.":"Cuanto más fresco, más ácida queda la uva y menos azúcar acumula.","With little heat and weaker sunshine, grapes ripen less: they build up less sugar and keep more acidity. In the glass this tends to give lighter, fresher wines. In a warm climate the opposite happens: more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours.":"Con poco calor y un sol más débil, la uva madura menos: acumula menos azúcar y conserva más acidez. En la copa, esto suele dar vinos más ligeros y frescos. En un clima cálido ocurre lo contrario: más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros.","Why does a warm-climate wine tend to show riper fruit flavours?":"¿Por qué un vino de clima cálido suele tener sabores de fruta más maduros?","Heat ripens the grapes further":"El calor hace madurar más la uva","Heat raises the grapes' acidity":"El calor aumenta la acidez de la uva","Heat removes colour from the skins":"El calor quita color a las pieles","Heat stops the vine flowering":"El calor detiene la floración","More heat and sun ripen grapes further: more sugar, riper flavours.":"Con más calor y sol la uva madura más: más azúcar y sabores más maduros.","In warm regions average temperatures are high and the sunshine is intense, so grapes ripen fully and reliably. This brings more sugar, less acidity and riper flavours. Chardonnay, for example, moves from apple and lemon aromas in a cool climate to peach and pineapple in a warm one.":"En las regiones cálidas las temperaturas medias son altas y el sol es intenso, así que la uva madura del todo y con regularidad. Esto aporta más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros. La Chardonnay, por ejemplo, pasa de aromas de manzana y limón en clima fresco a melocotón y piña en clima cálido.","A Chardonnay with apple and lemon aromas most likely comes from…":"Una Chardonnay con aromas de manzana y limón probablemente procede de…","A cool climate":"Un clima fresco","A warm climate":"Un clima cálido","A tropical climate":"Un clima tropical","A very dry climate":"Un clima muy seco","Green fruit and citrus point to less ripe, cool-climate grapes.":"La fruta verde y los cítricos indican uva menos madura, típica del clima fresco.","Climate changes the type of fruit you find in a wine. In a cool climate Chardonnay gives green fruit such as apple and citrus such as lemon. In a warm climate, with riper grapes, it shows stone fruit such as peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"El clima cambia el tipo de fruta que se percibe en el vino. En clima fresco, la Chardonnay da fruta verde como la manzana y cítricos como el limón. En clima cálido, con uva más madura, muestra fruta de hueso como el melocotón y fruta tropical como la piña.","Why can grapes in cool regions struggle to ripen in some years?":"¿Por qué en las regiones frescas a la uva le cuesta a veces madurar?","Low temperatures and weaker sunlight":"Temperaturas bajas y sol más débil","High temperatures and stronger sunlight":"Temperaturas altas y sol más intenso","Winters too mild for the vine to rest":"Inviernos demasiado suaves para descansar","Vines too young to flower":"Vides demasiado jóvenes para florecer","Little heat and weaker light slow down ripening.":"Poco calor y una luz más débil frenan la maduración.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there.":"Las regiones frescas están más cerca de los polos: las temperaturas medias son bajas y la luz del sol puede ser menos intensa que cerca del ecuador. En los años especialmente frescos la uva puede no llegar a madurar del todo. Por eso allí se cultivan a menudo uvas blancas.","After planting, how long does a vine usually take before it gives a crop every year?":"Tras plantarla, ¿cuánto tarda normalmente una vid en dar cosecha cada año?","A couple of years":"Un par de años","A few months":"Unos meses","About twenty years":"Unos veinte años","Half a century":"Medio siglo","A vine matures a couple of years after planting, then crops every year.":"Una vid madura un par de años después de plantarla y luego da cosecha cada año.","The vine is a long-lived plant that can survive for several decades. After planting it needs a couple of years to become mature; from then on it gives a crop every year, always following the same cycle: flowering in spring, ripening in summer and harvest in late summer.":"La vid es una planta longeva que puede vivir varias décadas. Tras plantarla necesita un par de años para llegar a la madurez; desde entonces da una cosecha cada año, siguiendo siempre el mismo ciclo: floración en primavera, maduración en verano y vendimia al final del verano.","Black grape skin":"Piel de la uva tinta","Deep colour and tannins, which make the mouth feel dry.":"Color intenso y taninos, que dejan la boca seca.","Grape pulp":"Pulpa de la uva","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes.":"Parte blanda con el zumo: agua, azúcar y ácido. Mismo color en todas las uvas.","Tannins":"Taninos","Substances in black grape skins that dry out the mouth.":"Sustancias de la piel de las uvas tintas que secan la boca.","The vine's yearly cycle":"Ciclo anual de la vid","Flowering in spring, ripening in summer, picking in late summer.":"Floración en primavera, maduración en verano, vendimia a finales de verano.","What changes as grapes ripen?":"¿Qué cambia cuando la uva madura?","More water and sugar, less acid, riper flavours, colour change.":"Más agua y azúcar, menos ácido, sabores más maduros, cambio de color.","Cool climate":"Clima fresco","Nearer the poles (Germany, northern France): less sugar, more acidity; often white grapes.":"Cerca de los polos (Alemania, norte de Francia): menos azúcar, más acidez; a menudo uvas blancas.","Warm climate":"Clima cálido","Nearer the Equator (parts of Australia and California): more sugar, less acidity, riper flavours; often black grapes.":"Cerca del ecuador (partes de Australia y California): más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores maduros; a menudo uvas tintas.","Chardonnay: cool or warm climate?":"Chardonnay: ¿clima fresco o cálido?","Cool: apple and lemon. Warm: peach and pineapple.":"Fresco: manzana y limón. Cálido: melocotón y piña.","Three types of wine: still, sparkling, fortified":"Tres tipos de vino: tranquilo, espumoso, fortificado","When people simply say «wine», they usually mean a still wine: one without bubbles. This is by far the biggest category. Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, though most sit between 11.5% and 14%. The abv figure (alcohol by volume) tells you how much of the liquid is alcohol, so a wine at 10% abv is one tenth alcohol.":"Cuando alguien dice simplemente «vino», casi siempre piensa en un vino tranquilo, es decir, sin burbujas. Es la categoría más amplia con diferencia. Los vinos tranquilos tienen entre un 8 % y un 15 % vol., aunque la mayoría se mueve entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %. La cifra «% vol.» (abv en inglés) indica qué parte del líquido es alcohol: un vino de 10 % vol. es una décima parte alcohol.","Many still wines take their name from the place where they are made: Sancerre and Burgundy in France, Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy. Others carry the name of the grape variety instead, such as a Pinot Grigio. Spotting which of the two naming logics a label uses is a quick first step towards knowing what will be in the glass.":"Muchos vinos tranquilos llevan el nombre de la zona donde se elaboran: Sancerre y Burgundy (Borgoña) en Francia, Rioja en España, Chianti en Italia. Otros, en cambio, indican el nombre de la variedad de uva, como un Pinot Grigio. Reconocer cuál de las dos lógicas sigue una etiqueta ayuda enseguida a saber qué esperar de la copa.","Sparkling wines are fizzy. Fermentation creates carbon dioxide gas, and if that gas is kept trapped inside the wine, it is released as bubbles once the bottle is opened. Champagne from France is the most famous example; Cava from Spain and Prosecco from Italy are also very well known. Sparkling wine is now made all around the world.":"Los vinos espumosos tienen burbujas. La fermentación genera dióxido de carbono y, si ese gas queda atrapado en el vino, sale en forma de burbujas al abrir la botella. El ejemplo más famoso es el Champagne francés; el Cava español y el Prosecco italiano también son muy conocidos. Hoy se elaboran espumosos en todo el mundo.","Fortified wines have had extra alcohol added to them. That is why they are stronger than still wines, usually somewhere between 15% and 22% abv. Two classic examples to remember are Sherry, from Spain, and Port, from Portugal. You will meet both again in the chapter on other wines to know.":"Los vinos fortificados son vinos a los que se ha añadido alcohol. Por eso tienen más graduación que los tranquilos: normalmente entre un 15 % y un 22 % vol. Dos ejemplos clásicos que conviene recordar son el Sherry (Jerez), de España, y el Port (Oporto), de Portugal. Volveremos a ellos en el capítulo de otros vinos que conocer.","Still: no bubbles, 8–15% abv (mostly 11.5–14%)":"Tranquilo: sin burbujas, 8–15 % vol. (casi siempre 11,5–14 %)","Sparkling: carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"Espumoso: dióxido de carbono de la fermentación atrapado en el vino","Fortified: extra alcohol added, 15–22% abv (Sherry, Port)":"Fortificado: alcohol añadido, 15–22 % vol. (Sherry, Port)","A wine may be named after its region or its grape":"Un vino puede llamarse como su zona o como su uva","Colour: white, red, rosé":"El color: blanco, tinto, rosado","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins.":"El color de un vino depende de dos cosas: la variedad de uva y la forma de elaborarlo. Hay uvas blancas y uvas tintas, pero por dentro se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color en ambas y el zumo es incoloro. Todo el color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo (la piel), que además contiene los taninos.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white.":"Los vinos blancos suelen elaborarse con uvas blancas, como un Chablis o un Riesling. Sin embargo, también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. Basta con separar los hollejos del zumo antes de la fermentación, por ejemplo con un prensado suave: como el color está en la piel, el zumo sigue claro y el vino resulta blanco.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples.":"Un vino tinto, en cambio, tiene que hacerse con uvas tintas. Durante la fermentación los hollejos permanecen en el zumo y se mezclan bien con él, de modo que le ceden color y tanino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino se separa de los hollejos. El Rioja español y los vinos de Cabernet Sauvignon son ejemplos de tintos.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak.":"El rosado también procede de uvas tintas, pero el contacto con los hollejos es breve: apenas unas horas. Después el zumo, solo ligeramente rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. El resultado es un vino de color suave. El White Zinfandel de California es un ejemplo de rosado. Además, los rosados rara vez se crían en roble.","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless":"El color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo; el zumo es incoloro","White: usually white grapes, possible from black grapes without skins":"Blanco: normalmente uvas blancas, también tintas sin hollejos","Red: black grapes only, skins kept through fermentation":"Tinto: solo uvas tintas, con hollejos durante toda la fermentación","Rosé: black grapes, a few hours of skin contact":"Rosado: uvas tintas, pocas horas de contacto con los hollejos","Structure (1): sweetness and acidity":"Estructura (1): dulzor y acidez","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds.":"El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino. La mayoría de los vinos son secos: para lograrlo, las levaduras tienen que convertir en alcohol todo el azúcar del zumo, de modo que queda muy poco o nada. Son secos, por ejemplo, el Chablis y los Sauvignon Blanc entre los blancos, y el Côtes du Rhône, el Chianti y los Cabernet Sauvignon entre los tintos.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples.":"Los vinos de dulzor medio son sobre todo blancos o rosados. Se elaboran de dos maneras: retirando las levaduras antes de que hayan transformado todo el azúcar, o añadiendo zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Algunos Riesling alemanes y el White Zinfandel, el rosado californiano, son buenos ejemplos.","Sweet wines hold so much sugar that they can feel thick, almost syrupy. They can come from grapes so rich in sugar that the yeast stop before eating it all, as in Sauternes or some German Rieslings. In fortified wines, strong distilled alcohol is added, killing the yeast early; the sugar left behind makes Port and some Sherries sweet.":"Los vinos dulces tienen tanto azúcar que pueden resultar espesos, casi como un almíbar. Pueden proceder de uvas tan azucaradas que las levaduras se detienen antes de consumirlo todo, como en el Sauternes o en algunos Riesling alemanes. En los fortificados, en cambio, se añade alcohol destilado de alta graduación que mata las levaduras: el azúcar restante hace dulces el Port y algunos Sherry.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity.":"La acidez procede directamente del zumo de uva y es lo que hace que un vino resulte refrescante. Es fácil de reconocer porque hace salivar. Demasiada acidez hace que el vino sea desagradablemente ácido; demasiado poca y pierde su frescura. El Chablis, el Chianti y los vinos de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon y Pinot Noir tienen acidez alta.","In sweet wines, acidity is vital. It acts as a counterweight to the sugar and stops the wine from tasting cloying. That is why a good Sauternes or a sweet Riesling always has high acidity: sweetness and freshness balance each other, and every sip stays enjoyable to the end.":"En los vinos dulces, la acidez es esencial. Hace de contrapeso al azúcar y evita que el vino resulte empalagoso. Por eso un buen Sauternes o un Riesling dulce siempre tienen una acidez alta: dulzor y frescura se equilibran y cada sorbo sigue siendo agradable hasta el final.","Dry: yeast turn all the sugar into alcohol":"Seco: las levaduras convierten todo el azúcar en alcohol","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added":"Medio: levaduras retiradas antes, o zumo sin fermentar añadido","Sweet: very sugary grapes, or added alcohol killing the yeast":"Dulce: uvas muy azucaradas, o alcohol añadido que mata las levaduras","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness":"Acidez: viene del zumo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor","Structure (2): tannin, alcohol and body":"Estructura (2): tanino, alcohol y cuerpo","Tannin belongs to red wines and comes from the skins of black grapes. How much a wine has depends on the grape variety and on the winemaking. It can taste a little bitter, but mostly it is something you feel: it leaves your mouth dry. Red Bordeaux and Chianti are high in tannin; Beaujolais and some Pinot Noir wines are low.":"El tanino es propio de los vinos tintos y procede de los hollejos de las uvas tintas. Su cantidad depende de la variedad y de la elaboración. Puede resultar algo amargo, pero sobre todo se nota como una sensación: deja la boca seca. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti tienen mucho tanino; el Beaujolais y algunos Pinot Noir, poco.","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar.":"Casi todos los vinos tranquilos y espumosos tienen entre un 11,5 % y un 14 % vol. Algunos llegan al 15 % y otros bajan hasta el 8 %. El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto francés, es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol; el White Zinfandel californiano, de vino con poco. Recuerda que el alcohol se forma cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar.","Body describes the overall feel of a wine in your mouth. Many things contribute to it, so the easiest question to ask is: how mouth-filling is it? Full-bodied wines feel dense and rich, while light-bodied ones feel more delicate. Light: Pinot Grigio, Beaujolais. Medium: Sancerre, Côtes du Rhône. Full: Californian Cabernet Sauvignon, Sauternes.":"El cuerpo describe la sensación general del vino en la boca. Influyen muchos factores, así que la pregunta más sencilla es: ¿cuánto llena la boca? Un vino con cuerpo parece denso y envolvente; uno ligero, más delicado. Ligeros: Pinot Grigio y Beaujolais. Medios: Sancerre y Côtes du Rhône. Con mucho cuerpo: Cabernet Sauvignon de California y Sauternes.","Tannin: from skins, dries the mouth, a red-wine feature":"Tanino: de los hollejos, seca la boca, propio de los tintos","Alcohol: usually 11.5–14% abv, 8–15% for still and sparkling":"Alcohol: normalmente 11,5–14 % vol., entre 8 y 15 % en tranquilos y espumosos","Body: how mouth-filling the wine is (light, medium, full)":"Cuerpo: cuánto llena la boca el vino (ligero, medio, con cuerpo)","Aromas and flavours: fruit, oak, other":"Aromas y sabores: fruta, roble, otros","A wine's aromas and flavours come from different places. Some come straight from the grapes, while others develop during winemaking and maturation. Putting them into words feels hard at first, but it is a skill that grows with practice. A simple method is to ask three questions: do I notice fruit? Oak? Something else?":"Los aromas y sabores de un vino tienen orígenes distintos. Algunos proceden directamente de la uva y otros aparecen durante la elaboración y la crianza. Al principio cuesta describirlos, pero es una habilidad que mejora con la práctica. Un método sencillo es preguntarse: ¿noto fruta? ¿Noto roble? ¿Noto otra cosa?","Almost every wine smells of fruit. The kind of fruit depends first on the grape variety: Cabernet Sauvignon, for instance, smells of blackcurrant. Ripeness matters too. A Chardonnay from a cool climate shows green apple and lemon, whereas one from a warm climate leans towards peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple.":"Casi todos los vinos huelen a fruta. El tipo de fruta depende ante todo de la variedad: el Cabernet Sauvignon, por ejemplo, recuerda a la grosella negra. También influye la madurez de la uva: un Chardonnay de clima fresco recuerda a la manzana verde y al limón, mientras que uno de clima cálido tira hacia el melocotón y frutas tropicales como la piña.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel.":"El vino puede fermentar y/o criarse en barricas de roble. En ese caso la madera aporta notas de vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y ahumado. A veces el uso de roble aparece en la etiqueta. Si notas estos aromas junto a la fruta, es una buena pista de que el vino ha pasado por barrica.","Finally, there are the «other» aromas that make wine so varied and interesting: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. A Sauvignon Blanc, for example, can bring cut grass to mind, while Chianti can show dried herbs. Keeping them in a family of their own stops you confusing them with fruit.":"Por último están los «otros» aromas, que hacen el vino tan variado e interesante: hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, champiñón y cuero. Un Sauvignon Blanc, por ejemplo, puede recordar a hierba recién cortada, y el Chianti a hierbas secas. Agruparlos en una familia aparte ayuda a no confundirlos con la fruta.","Fruit: depends on the grape variety and its ripeness":"Fruta: depende de la variedad y de la madurez de la uva","Cool climate = apple, lemon; warm climate = peach, pineapple":"Clima fresco = manzana, limón; clima cálido = melocotón, piña","Oak: vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke":"Roble: vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro, ahumado","Other: grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom, leather":"Otros: hierba, flores, hierbas, verduras, tierra, champiñón, cuero","Style: the sum of the characteristics":"El estilo: la suma de las características","Each of the three types of wine, still, sparkling or fortified, can come in many different styles. A style brings together three elements: colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. Describing a style means putting these pieces together into one complete portrait of the wine.":"Cada uno de los tres tipos de vino, tranquilo, espumoso o fortificado, puede presentarse en muchos estilos. El estilo reúne tres elementos: el color, la estructura (dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo) y los aromas y sabores. Describir un estilo es juntar estas piezas en un retrato completo del vino.","A comparison makes this clear. Chablis and Sauternes are both French white wines, yet their styles are opposites. Chablis is dry, high in acidity, light to medium in body, with green apple and lemon and no oak. Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla from oak, held up by high acidity.":"Una comparación lo deja claro. El Chablis y el Sauternes son ambos blancos franceses y, sin embargo, sus estilos son opuestos. El Chablis es seco, de acidez alta, cuerpo ligero a medio, con manzana verde y limón y sin roble. El Sauternes es dulce y con cuerpo, con albaricoque, miel y vainilla del roble, sostenido por una acidez alta.","Style depends a lot on the climate where the grapes grow. The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acidity the grapes have, giving fresher, lighter wines with green fruit and citrus. The warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity: flavours taste riper and, since sugar becomes alcohol, wines tend to be stronger and fuller.":"El estilo depende mucho del clima en que crece la uva. Cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tiene la uva: salen vinos más frescos y ligeros, con fruta verde y cítricos. Cuanto más cálido, más azúcar y menos acidez: los sabores son más maduros y, como el azúcar se convierte en alcohol, los vinos suelen tener más graduación y más cuerpo.","To describe a style, you follow a systematic approach to tasting. First the appearance: the colour (white, red, rosé). Then the nose: aromas of fruit, oak or other. Finally the palate: sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol and body, plus the flavours. Always using the same order makes it easier to compare wines and remember them.":"Para describir un estilo se sigue un enfoque sistemático de la cata. Primero la vista: el color (blanco, tinto, rosado). Después la nariz: aromas de fruta, de roble u otros. Por último la boca: dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol y cuerpo, además de los sabores. Seguir siempre el mismo orden ayuda a quien estudia a comparar vinos y recordarlos.","Style = colour + structure + aromas and flavours":"Estilo = color + estructura + aromas y sabores","Cool climate: more acid, less sugar, lighter and fresher wines":"Clima fresco: más acidez, menos azúcar, vinos más ligeros y frescos","Warm climate: more sugar, less acid, riper flavours":"Clima cálido: más azúcar, menos acidez, sabores más maduros","Tasting: appearance, nose, palate, always in the same order":"Cata: vista, nariz, boca, siempre en el mismo orden","Which type of wine has had extra alcohol added?":"¿A qué tipo de vino se le ha añadido alcohol?","Fortified":"Fortificado","Sparkling":"Espumoso","Still":"Tranquilo","Rosé":"Rosado","Fortified wines have alcohol added, which makes them stronger.":"A los fortificados se les añade alcohol, por eso son más fuertes.","There are three types of wine: still, sparkling and fortified. Only fortified wine has extra alcohol added, which lifts it to between 15% and 22% abv. Sparkling wine owes its bubbles to carbon dioxide from fermentation, and rosé is a colour, not a type of wine.":"Hay tres tipos de vino: tranquilo, espumoso y fortificado. Solo al fortificado se le añade alcohol, lo que eleva su graduación a entre el 15 % y el 22 % vol. El espumoso debe sus burbujas al dióxido de carbono de la fermentación, y el rosado es un color, no un tipo de vino.","What is the usual alcohol range of fortified wines?":"¿Cuál es la graduación habitual de los vinos fortificados?","15–22% abv":"15–22 % vol.","8–11% abv":"8–11 % vol.","11.5–14% abv":"11,5–14 % vol.","4–7% abv":"4–7 % vol.","The added alcohol puts fortified wines between 15% and 22% abv.":"El alcohol añadido sitúa a los fortificados entre el 15 % y el 22 % vol.","Still and sparkling wines almost always sit between 11.5% and 14% abv, with extremes from 8% to 15%. Fortified wines such as Sherry and Port have extra alcohol added, so they move up into a higher band of 15% to 22% abv.":"Los vinos tranquilos y espumosos casi siempre están entre el 11,5 % y el 14 % vol., con extremos del 8 % al 15 %. Los fortificados, como el Sherry y el Port, reciben alcohol adicional y suben a una franja más alta, del 15 % al 22 % vol.","Where do the bubbles in sparkling wine come from?":"¿De dónde salen las burbujas del vino espumoso?","Carbon dioxide from fermentation trapped in the wine":"Dióxido de carbono de la fermentación atrapado en el vino","Distilled alcohol added after fermentation":"Alcohol destilado añadido tras la fermentación","Sugar left in the wine after fermentation":"Azúcar que queda en el vino tras fermentar","Air entering through the oak barrel staves":"Aire que entra por las duelas de la barrica","Fermentation makes carbon dioxide; when it is trapped, it becomes the bubbles.":"La fermentación produce dióxido de carbono; si queda atrapado, forma las burbujas.","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol and carbon dioxide. In still wines the gas escapes into the air, but in sparkling wines it is kept inside the wine. When the bottle is opened, the gas is released as bubbles, as in Champagne, Cava or Prosecco.":"Las levaduras convierten el azúcar en alcohol y dióxido de carbono. En los vinos tranquilos el gas se escapa al aire, pero en los espumosos se retiene dentro del vino. Al abrir la botella, el gas se libera en forma de burbujas, como en el Champagne, el Cava o el Prosecco.","Between which values do most still wines fall?":"¿Entre qué valores se sitúan la mayoría de los vinos tranquilos?","11.5% and 14% abv":"11,5 % y 14 % vol.","15% and 22% abv":"15 % y 22 % vol.","5% and 8% abv":"5 % y 8 % vol.","16% and 20% abv":"16 % y 20 % vol.","Still wines range from 8% to 15% abv, but most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"Los tranquilos van del 8 % al 15 % vol., pero casi todos entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %.","The full range for still wines runs from 8% to 15% abv, but the great majority sit between 11.5% and 14%. Figures of 15% to 22% are typical of fortified wines, which have alcohol added. White Zinfandel is an example of a still wine at the low end.":"La franja completa de los vinos tranquilos va del 8 % al 15 % vol., pero la gran mayoría se sitúa entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %. Las cifras del 15 % al 22 % son típicas de los fortificados, a los que se añade alcohol. El White Zinfandel es un ejemplo de vino con poca graduación.","Which of these wines is named after its grape variety?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos lleva el nombre de su variedad de uva?","Pinot Grigio":"Pinot Grigio","Rioja":"Rioja","Chianti":"Chianti","Sancerre":"Sancerre","Pinot Grigio is a grape; Rioja, Chianti and Sancerre are places.":"Pinot Grigio es una uva; Rioja, Chianti y Sancerre son zonas.","Many European wines take the name of the area where they are made: Rioja in Spain, Chianti in Italy, Sancerre in France. Other wines show the grape variety on the label instead. Pinot Grigio is a typical example of a wine named after its grape.":"Muchos vinos europeos llevan el nombre de la zona donde se elaboran: Rioja en España, Chianti en Italia, Sancerre en Francia. Otros, en cambio, indican la variedad de uva en la etiqueta. El Pinot Grigio es precisamente un ejemplo de vino que se llama como su uva.","Which of these is a Spanish sparkling wine?":"¿Cuál de estos es un espumoso español?","Cava":"Cava","Prosecco":"Prosecco","Champagne":"Champagne","Sherry":"Sherry","Cava is the sparkling wine from Spain.":"El Cava es el espumoso de España.","Three famous sparkling wines to remember: Champagne from France, Prosecco from Italy and Cava from Spain. Sherry is also Spanish, but it is a fortified wine, not a sparkling one: it has had alcohol added and has no bubbles. Sparkling wines are, in fact, now made in almost every wine-producing country.":"Tres espumosos famosos que conviene recordar: Champagne de Francia, Prosecco de Italia y Cava de España. El Sherry también es español, pero es un vino fortificado, no un espumoso: lleva alcohol añadido y no tiene burbujas. De hecho, hoy se elaboran espumosos en casi todos los países productores de vino.","Why is a red wine red?":"¿Por qué un vino tinto es tinto?","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation":"Los hollejos se quedan en el zumo durante la fermentación","The pulp of black grapes is red in colour":"La pulpa de las uvas tintas es de color rojo","The oak barrels give their colour to the wine":"Las barricas de roble ceden color al vino","Unfermented black grape juice is added":"Se añade zumo de uva tinta sin fermentar","The colour is in the skins, which release it during fermentation.":"El color está en los hollejos, que lo ceden durante la fermentación.","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine.":"La pulpa de las uvas blancas y tintas tiene el mismo color y el zumo es incoloro. Para hacer un tinto se usan uvas tintas y se dejan los hollejos en contacto con el zumo durante toda la fermentación, mezclándolos bien: así pasan al vino el color y el tanino.","Can a white wine be made from black grapes?":"¿Se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas?","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation":"Sí, separando hollejos y zumo antes de fermentar","Yes, but only if the wine is then aged in oak":"Sí, pero solo si después se cría en roble","No, black grapes always give a red wine":"No, las uvas tintas siempre dan vino tinto","No, black grapes can only make rosé wine":"No, las uvas tintas solo dan vino rosado","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white.":"El zumo de la uva tinta es incoloro: sin hollejos, el vino queda blanco.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne.":"Todo el color de la uva tinta está en su piel. Si las uvas se prensan con suavidad y los hollejos se separan del zumo antes de la fermentación, el zumo sigue claro y da un vino blanco. Es la misma idea que permite usar Pinot Noir en el Champagne.","How is a rosé wine made?":"¿Cómo se elabora un vino rosado?","Black grapes with only a few hours of skin contact":"Uvas tintas con pocas horas de contacto con los hollejos","White grapes fermented together with their skins":"Uvas blancas fermentadas junto con sus hollejos","Black grapes kept on skins until fermentation ends":"Uvas tintas con hollejos hasta el final de la fermentación","White grapes aged for a long time in oak barrels":"Uvas blancas criadas largo tiempo en barricas de roble","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off.":"El zumo pasa unas horas con los hollejos de uva tinta y luego se separa.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead.":"El rosado procede de uvas tintas, como el tinto, pero el contacto con los hollejos dura solo unas horas. El zumo, apenas rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. Si los hollejos se quedaran hasta el final, se obtendría un vino tinto.","Which of these wines is a rosé?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos es un rosado?","White Zinfandel":"White Zinfandel","Chablis":"Chablis","Beaujolais":"Beaujolais","Sauternes":"Sauternes","Despite its name, White Zinfandel from California is a rosé.":"Pese a su nombre, el White Zinfandel de California es un rosado.","The name can mislead you: White Zinfandel is a Californian rosé, medium-sweet, low in alcohol, with strawberry and raspberry flavours. Chablis and Sauternes are French white wines, while Beaujolais is a light red with low tannin. So never judge a wine by its name alone.":"El nombre puede despistar: el White Zinfandel es un rosado californiano, de dulzor medio, con poco alcohol y sabores de fresa y frambuesa. El Chablis y el Sauternes son blancos franceses, y el Beaujolais es un tinto ligero y con poco tanino. Así que conviene no juzgar nunca un vino solo por su nombre.","What happens when a dry wine is made?":"¿Qué ocurre cuando se elabora un vino seco?","The yeast turn all of the sugar into alcohol":"Las levaduras convierten todo el azúcar en alcohol","Distilled alcohol is added before fermentation ends":"Se añade alcohol destilado antes del final","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine":"Se añade zumo de uva sin fermentar","The yeast are removed before they finish":"Se retiran las levaduras antes de terminar","A wine is dry when the yeast have eaten all the sugar.":"Un vino es seco cuando las levaduras se han comido todo el azúcar.","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines.":"La mayoría de los vinos son secos: las levaduras trabajan hasta convertir todo el azúcar en alcohol. Las demás respuestas describen formas de conservar azúcar: retirar las levaduras o añadir zumo en los vinos de dulzor medio, y añadir alcohol en los fortificados dulces.","Which method is used to make a medium-sweet wine?":"¿Qué método sirve para obtener un vino de dulzor medio?","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine":"Añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer":"Dejar los hollejos más tiempo en el zumo","Maturing the wine in oak barrels":"Criar el vino en barricas de roble","Picking the grapes before they ripen":"Vendimiar la uva antes de que madure","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine.":"El zumo sin fermentar aporta azúcar a un vino ya seco.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness.":"Hay dos caminos para un vino de dulzor medio: retirar las levaduras antes de que consuman todo el azúcar, o añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Los hollejos y el roble influyen en el color, el tanino y los aromas, no en el dulzor.","In a sweet fortified wine, what stops the fermentation?":"En un vino fortificado dulce, ¿qué detiene la fermentación?","Adding distilled alcohol, which kills the yeast":"Añadir alcohol destilado, que mata las levaduras","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine":"Añadir zumo de uva sin fermentar","Moving the wine into oak barrels":"Pasar el vino a barricas de roble","Draining the wine off the skins":"Separar el vino de los hollejos","The strong added alcohol kills the yeast, leaving sugar in the wine.":"El alcohol fuerte añadido mata las levaduras y deja azúcar en el vino.","In sweet fortified wines, high-strength distilled alcohol is added before the yeast have eaten all the sugar. The yeast die, the leftover sugar makes the wine sweet and the added alcohol makes it stronger. Port and some Sherries are made this way.":"En los fortificados dulces se añade alcohol destilado de alta graduación antes de que las levaduras se coman todo el azúcar. Las levaduras mueren, el azúcar que queda hace dulce el vino y el alcohol añadido lo hace más fuerte. Así se elaboran el Port y algunos Sherry.","Which sensation tells you a wine has high acidity?":"¿Qué sensación indica una acidez alta?","It makes your mouth water":"Hace salivar","It makes your mouth feel dry":"Deja la boca seca","It warms the back of your throat":"Da calor en la garganta","It feels thick and syrupy":"Parece espesa y almibarada","Acidity is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water.":"La acidez se reconoce porque hace salivar.","Each part of a wine's structure has its own sensation. Acidity makes your mouth water and brings freshness. Tannin, by contrast, dries the mouth; alcohol is felt as warmth; and a very sweet wine can feel thick and syrupy. Too much acidity, however, makes a wine taste unpleasantly sharp.":"Cada elemento de la estructura se reconoce por una sensación distinta. La acidez hace salivar y aporta frescura. El tanino, en cambio, seca la boca; el alcohol se nota como calor; y un vino muy dulce puede resultar espeso y almibarado. Eso sí, demasiada acidez hace que el vino resulte desagradablemente ácido.","Why is acidity important in sweet wines?":"¿Por qué es importante la acidez en los vinos dulces?","It balances the sweetness so the wine is not cloying":"Equilibra el dulzor y evita que empalague","It raises the alcohol level of the wine":"Aumenta la graduación del vino","It gives the wine a deeper colour":"Da al vino un color más intenso","It adds tannin and therefore more body":"Añade tanino y, por tanto, más cuerpo","Without acidity, a sweet wine would taste cloying.":"Sin acidez, un vino dulce resultaría empalagoso.","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy.":"La acidez procede del zumo de uva y refresca el vino. En los dulces hace de contrapeso al azúcar: por eso el Sauternes y los Riesling dulces tienen acidez alta. No influye en el color, el tanino ni la graduación. Sin ella, el vino resultaría pesado.","Where does tannin in wine come from?":"¿De dónde procede el tanino del vino?","The skins of black grapes":"Los hollejos de la uva tinta","The pulp of white grapes":"La pulpa de la uva blanca","The sugar in the juice":"El azúcar del zumo","The yeast used in fermentation":"Las levaduras de la fermentación","Tannin sits in black grape skins, which is why it is a red-wine feature.":"El tanino está en el hollejo de la uva tinta; por eso es propio de los tintos.","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little.":"Las uvas tintas tienen hollejos coloreados que contienen taninos. Al fermentar un tinto, los hollejos permanecen en el zumo y le ceden color y tanino. La cantidad final depende de la variedad y de la elaboración: el Bordeaux tinto tiene mucho; el Beaujolais, poco.","Which of these reds is low in tannin?":"¿Cuál de estos tintos tiene poco tanino?","Red Bordeaux":"Bordeaux tinto","Port":"Port","Beaujolais is a light, fresh red with low tannin.":"El Beaujolais es un tinto ligero, fresco y con poco tanino.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry.":"El Beaujolais es un ejemplo clásico de tinto con poco tanino, como algunos Pinot Noir. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti, en cambio, son ejemplos típicos de tintos muy tánicos, y el Port, vino fortificado tinto y dulce, también tiene taninos altos. Recuerda que el tanino deja la boca seca.","Which of these is an example of a high-alcohol wine?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol?","Châteauneuf-du-Pape":"Châteauneuf-du-Pape","Châteauneuf-du-Pape is a full-bodied French red with high alcohol.":"El Châteauneuf-du-Pape es un tinto francés con cuerpo y mucho alcohol.","Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a red from the Rhône, is the textbook example of a high-alcohol wine: dry and full-bodied, with strawberry and clove. At the other end, White Zinfandel is the standard low-alcohol example, while Beaujolais and Pinot Grigio are light-bodied wines.":"El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto del Ródano, es el ejemplo típico de vino con mucho alcohol: seco, con cuerpo, con fresa y clavo. En el extremo opuesto, el White Zinfandel es el ejemplo de vino con poco alcohol, y el Beaujolais y el Pinot Grigio son vinos ligeros.","What does «12% abv» on a label mean?":"¿Qué significa «12 % vol.» en la etiqueta?","12% of the liquid is alcohol":"El 12 % del líquido es alcohol","The wine contains 12% sugar":"El vino contiene un 12 % de azúcar","12% of the grapes were black":"El 12 % de la uva era tinta","The wine spent 12 months in oak":"El vino pasó 12 meses en barrica","Alcohol by volume shows what share of the wine is alcohol.":"El porcentaje en volumen indica qué parte del vino es alcohol.","Alcohol is measured as a percentage of the total volume, called alcohol by volume or abv. A wine at 12% abv has twelve parts alcohol in every hundred. That is a typical figure for a still wine, as most sit between 11.5% and 14%.":"El alcohol se mide como porcentaje del volumen total (abv en inglés). Un vino de 12 % vol. contiene doce partes de alcohol de cada cien. Es una cifra típica de un vino tranquilo: la mayoría se sitúa entre el 11,5 % y el 14 %.","What does the body of a wine describe?":"¿Qué describe el cuerpo de un vino?","How mouth-filling the wine feels":"Cuánto llena la boca el vino","How much acidity the wine contains":"Cuánta acidez contiene el vino","How deep the colour of the wine is":"Lo intenso que es el color del vino","How long the wine stayed in oak":"Cuánto tiempo pasó en barrica","Body is the overall feel in the mouth: light, medium or full.":"El cuerpo es la sensación general en boca: ligero, medio o con cuerpo.","Many factors shape body, so the practical question is: how much does this wine fill my mouth? Full-bodied wines such as Sauternes or a Californian Cabernet Sauvignon feel dense and rich, while light ones such as Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais feel more delicate.":"El cuerpo depende de muchos factores, así que la pregunta práctica es: ¿cuánto me llena la boca este vino? Los vinos con cuerpo, como el Sauternes o un Cabernet Sauvignon californiano, resultan densos; los ligeros, como el Pinot Grigio o el Beaujolais, más delicados.","Which of these wines is full-bodied?":"¿Cuál de estos vinos tiene mucho cuerpo?","Sauternes, the sweet white from Bordeaux, is full-bodied.":"El Sauternes, blanco dulce de Burdeos, tiene mucho cuerpo.","Sauternes is sweet and full-bodied, with apricot, honey and vanilla. Pinot Grigio and Beaujolais are examples of light-bodied wines, and Sancerre is a dry white with medium body. A Californian Cabernet Sauvignon would also be a good example of a full-bodied wine.":"El Sauternes es dulce y con mucho cuerpo, con albaricoque, miel y vainilla. El Pinot Grigio y el Beaujolais son ejemplos de vinos ligeros, y el Sancerre es un blanco seco de cuerpo medio. Un Cabernet Sauvignon de California también sería un buen ejemplo de vino con cuerpo.","Which group of aromas typically comes from oak?":"¿Qué grupo de aromas procede normalmente del roble?","Vanilla, cedar, smoke":"Vainilla, cedro, ahumado","Apple, lemon, pear":"Manzana, limón, pera","Grass, asparagus, bell pepper":"Hierba, espárrago, pimiento","Strawberry, raspberry, cherry":"Fresa, frambuesa, cereza","Oak gives vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves.":"El roble aporta vainilla, cedro, ahumado, coco y clavo.","When a wine is fermented or matured in oak barrels, the wood adds notes of vanilla, cedar, smoke, coconut and cloves. Apple, lemon and pear are fruit aromas, while grass, asparagus and bell pepper are herbaceous notes typical of Sauvignon Blanc, for example.":"Cuando un vino fermenta o se cría en barricas de roble, la madera aporta notas de vainilla, cedro, ahumado, coco y clavo. Manzana, limón y pera son aromas de fruta; hierba, espárrago y pimiento son notas herbáceas típicas, por ejemplo, del Sauvignon Blanc.","Which aromas does a cool-climate Chardonnay usually show?":"¿Qué aromas suele tener un Chardonnay de clima fresco?","Green apple and lemon":"Manzana verde y limón","Peach and pineapple":"Melocotón y piña","Blackcurrant and mint":"Grosella negra y menta","Strawberry and cherry":"Fresa y cereza","In a cool climate grapes ripen less, giving green fruit and citrus.":"En clima fresco la uva madura menos: fruta verde y cítricos.","How ripe the grapes are changes the fruit you notice. A cool-climate Chardonnay smells of green apple and lemon; a warm-climate one of peach and tropical fruit such as pineapple. Blackcurrant and mint are typical of Cabernet Sauvignon, and strawberry and cherry of Pinot Noir.":"La madurez de la uva cambia la fruta que se percibe. Un Chardonnay de clima fresco huele a manzana verde y limón; uno de clima cálido, a melocotón y frutas tropicales como la piña. Grosella negra y menta son típicas del Cabernet Sauvignon, y fresa y cereza del Pinot Noir.","Which of these aromas belongs to the «other» family?":"¿Cuál de estos aromas pertenece a la familia «otros»?","Mushroom":"Champiñón","Pineapple":"Piña","Vanilla":"Vainilla","Blackcurrant":"Grosella negra","Mushroom, earth, leather, grass and flowers are «other» aromas.":"Champiñón, tierra, cuero, hierba y flores son «otros» aromas.","Aromas fall into three families: fruit, oak and other. Pineapple and blackcurrant are fruit, and vanilla comes from oak. The «other» family covers grass, flowers, herbs, vegetables, earth, mushroom and leather. These are the aromas that make wine so varied and interesting to explore.":"Los aromas se reparten en tres familias: fruta, roble y otros. La piña y la grosella negra son fruta, y la vainilla procede del roble. La familia «otros» agrupa hierba, flores, hierbas aromáticas, verduras, tierra, champiñón y cuero. Son precisamente estos aromas los que hacen el vino tan variado e interesante.","What is the style of a wine?":"¿Qué es el estilo de un vino?","Its colour, structure and aromas combined":"El conjunto de color, estructura y aromas","Only the grape variety it is made from":"Solo la variedad con la que se elabora","Only the region where it is produced":"Solo la zona donde se produce","Only its level of alcohol":"Solo su graduación alcohólica","Style combines colour, structure, and aromas and flavours.":"El estilo combina color, estructura y aromas y sabores.","Grape, region and alcohol all influence style, but none of them describes it alone. Style is the sum of colour, structure (sweetness, acidity, tannin, alcohol, body) and aromas and flavours. That is how two French whites such as Chablis and Sauternes can be complete opposites.":"La uva, la zona y el alcohol influyen en el estilo, pero ninguno lo describe por sí solo. El estilo es la suma del color, la estructura (dulzor, acidez, tanino, alcohol, cuerpo) y los aromas y sabores. Por eso dos blancos franceses como el Chablis y el Sauternes pueden ser opuestos.","What effect does a cool climate have on the grapes?":"¿Qué efecto tiene un clima fresco en la uva?","More tannin and more colour":"Más tanino y más color","Riper, more tropical flavours":"Sabores más maduros y tropicales","The cooler it is, the less sugar and the more acid the grapes have.":"Cuanto más fresco, menos azúcar y más acidez tiene la uva.","As a rule, the cooler the climate, the more acidic and the less sugary the grapes stay; the warmer it is, the more sugar and the less acidity, with riper flavours. That is why cool-climate wines tend to be fresher and lighter, with green fruit and citrus.":"En general, cuanto más fresco es el clima, más ácida y menos dulce se queda la uva; cuanto más cálido, más azúcar, menos acidez y sabores más maduros. Por eso los vinos de clima fresco suelen ser más frescos y ligeros, con fruta verde y cítricos.","Still wine":"Vino tranquilo","Wine without bubbles; 8–15% abv, mostly 11.5–14%.":"Vino sin burbujas; 8–15 % vol., casi siempre 11,5–14 %.","Sparkling wine":"Vino espumoso","Bubbles of carbon dioxide from fermentation. E.g. Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.":"Burbujas de dióxido de carbono de la fermentación. Ej.: Champagne, Cava, Prosecco.","Fortified wine":"Vino fortificado","Wine with added alcohol, 15–22% abv. E.g. Sherry, Port.":"Vino con alcohol añadido, 15–22 % vol. Ej.: Sherry, Port.","abv":"% vol. (abv)","Alcohol by volume: 10% means one tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"Porcentaje de alcohol en volumen: 10 % = una décima parte es alcohol.","Dry wine":"Vino seco","No or very little sugar: the yeast turned it all into alcohol.":"Nada o muy poco azúcar: las levaduras lo convirtieron todo en alcohol.","Acidity":"Acidez","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness.":"Viene del zumo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor.","Tannin":"Tanino","From black grape skins; dries the mouth. High: red Bordeaux, Chianti.":"De los hollejos de uva tinta; seca la boca. Alto: Bordeaux tinto, Chianti.","Body":"Cuerpo","How mouth-filling a wine is: light (Pinot Grigio), medium (Sancerre), full (Sauternes).":"Cuánto llena la boca: ligero (Pinot Grigio), medio (Sancerre), con cuerpo (Sauternes).","Oak aromas":"Aromas del roble","Vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar, smoke.":"Vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro, ahumado.","Rosé wine":"Vino rosado","Black grapes, a few hours on the skins, then fermented without them.":"Uvas tintas, unas horas con los hollejos y luego fermentación sin ellos.","Grapes, vines and climate":"La uva, la vid y el clima","How wine is made":"Cómo se hace el vino","Types and styles of wine":"Tipos y estilos de vino","The four key white grapes":"Las cuatro grandes blancas","The four key black grapes":"Las cuatro grandes tintas","Famous wines from the key grapes":"Vinos famosos de las uvas principales","Other wines to know":"Otros vinos que conocer","Storing and serving wine":"Conservar y servir el vino","Food and wine":"Comida y vino","Tasting: first steps":"Catar: primeros pasos","From vine to wine":"De la viña al vino","Types, styles and grapes":"Tipos, estilos y uvas","Store, serve, pair":"Conservar, servir, maridar"},"ar":{"Wine starts from a simple idea: crush grapes to free their sweet juice, then let that juice ferment. That is why wine can be described as fermented grape juice. To understand what ends up in the glass, it helps to start with the grape itself, which has two main parts: the skin on the outside and the pulp on the inside. Each one gives something different to the wine.":"El vino parte de una idea sencilla: se estrujan las uvas para liberar su jugo dulce y después se deja fermentar. Por eso el vino se puede definir como jugo de uva fermentado. Para entender lo que acabará en la copa, conviene empezar por la uva, que tiene dos partes principales: la piel por fuera y la pulpa por dentro. Cada una aporta algo distinto al vino.","The pulp is the soft, fleshy part of the grape and it holds the juice. That juice is made up mostly of water, sugar and acid. One important detail: the pulp has the same colour whether the grape is white or black. So the colour of a red wine does not come from the juice but from the skins, a key idea for understanding later how the different wines are made.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda y carnosa de la uva y es la que contiene el jugo. Ese jugo está formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Un detalle importante: la pulpa tiene el mismo color tanto en las uvas blancas como en las tintas. Por eso el color de un vino tinto no viene del jugo sino de las pieles, una idea clave para entender después cómo se elaboran los distintos vinos.","Wine is fermented grape juice.":"El vino es jugo de uva fermentado.","Pulp: juice made of water, sugar and acid.":"Pulpa: jugo de agua, azúcar y ácido.","Wine regions closer to the poles have a cool climate. Germany and northern France are typical examples. Average temperatures are low and the sunshine can be weaker than nearer the Equator; in some years the grapes even struggle to ripen. In cool climates, growing white grapes is common.":"Las regiones vitícolas más cercanas a los polos tienen un clima fresco. Alemania y el norte de Francia son ejemplos típicos. Allá las temperaturas medias son bajas y el sol puede ser más débil que cerca del ecuador; algunos años a la uva incluso le cuesta madurar. En los climas frescos es habitual cultivar uvas blancas.","Fermented grape juice":"Jugo de uva fermentado","Distilled grape juice":"Jugo de uva destilado","Concentrated grape juice":"Jugo de uva concentrado","Pasteurised grape juice":"Jugo de uva pasteurizado","Wine is made by fermenting the sweet juice of grapes.":"El vino se obtiene haciendo fermentar el jugo dulce de la uva.","To make wine, grapes are crushed to release their sweet juice. Alcoholic fermentation, carried out by yeast, then turns the sugar in that juice into alcohol. Without fermentation you would simply have grape juice; distilling or concentrating the juice is not part of the basic definition of wine.":"Para hacer vino se estrujan las uvas y se libera su jugo dulce. Después, la fermentación alcohólica, gracias a las levaduras, convierte el azúcar de ese jugo en alcohol. Sin fermentación solo quedaría jugo de uva; destilar o concentrar el jugo no forma parte de la definición básica del vino.","The juice":"En el jugo","The skin is what really sets black grapes apart from white ones: it is deeply coloured and contains tannins, which leave the mouth feeling dry. The pulp, by contrast, holds the juice, made of water, sugar and acid, and it is the same colour in all grapes.":"La piel es lo que distingue de verdad las uvas tintas de las blancas: tiene un color intenso y contiene taninos, que dejan sensación de sequedad en la boca. La pulpa, en cambio, contiene el jugo, formado por agua, azúcar y ácido, y tiene el mismo color en todas las uvas.","What is the juice in the pulp mainly made of?":"¿De qué está compuesto principalmente el jugo de la pulpa?","Grape juice is mostly water, sugar and acid.":"El jugo de uva es sobre todo agua, azúcar y ácido.","The pulp is the soft part of the grape and holds the juice, which is mostly water, sugar and acid. Tannin and colour are found in the skin instead. Alcohol and carbon dioxide only appear later, when yeast ferments the sugar in the juice.":"La pulpa es la parte blanda de la uva y contiene el jugo, formado sobre todo por agua, azúcar y ácido. Los taninos y el color están en la piel. El alcohol y el dióxido de carbono solo aparecen más tarde, cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar del jugo.","Inside, white and black grapes look very alike: the pulp is the same colour whatever the colour of the skin. This is exactly why a red wine gets its colour from the skins, and why a white wine can even be made from black grapes if the juice is separated from the skins straight away.":"Por dentro, las uvas blancas y tintas se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color sea cual sea el de la piel. Precisamente por eso el color de un vino tinto viene de las pieles, y por eso se puede hacer incluso un vino blanco con uvas tintas si se separa el jugo de las pieles enseguida.","Warm regions, closer to the Equator, have high average temperatures and more intense sunshine, so grapes ripen reliably. Growing black grapes is common there. In cool regions, closer to the poles, where grapes sometimes struggle to ripen at all, white grapes are more commonly grown.":"Las regiones cálidas, más cercanas al ecuador, tienen temperaturas medias altas y un sol más intenso, así que la uva madura con regularidad. Allá es habitual cultivar uvas tintas. En las regiones frescas, donde a veces a la uva le cuesta madurar, es más frecuente cultivar uvas blancas.","Cool regions lie closer to the poles: average temperatures are low and the sunlight can be less intense than near the Equator. In especially cool years the grapes may not ripen fully. This is one reason white grapes are commonly grown there.":"Las regiones frescas están más cerca de los polos: las temperaturas medias son bajas y la luz del sol puede ser menos intensa que cerca del ecuador. En los años especialmente frescos la uva puede no llegar a madurar del todo. Por eso allá se cultivan a menudo uvas blancas.","Soft part holding the juice: water, sugar and acid. Same colour in all grapes.":"Parte blanda con el jugo: agua, azúcar y ácido. Mismo color en todas las uvas.","A wine's colour depends on two things: the grape variety and the way the wine is made. There are white grapes and black grapes, but inside they look very alike: the pulp is the same colour in both and the juice has no colour. All the colour of a black grape sits in its skin, which also holds the tannins.":"El color de un vino depende de dos cosas: la variedad de uva y la forma de elaborarlo. Hay uvas blancas y uvas tintas, pero por dentro se parecen mucho: la pulpa tiene el mismo color en ambas y el jugo es incoloro. Todo el color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo (la piel), que además contiene los taninos.","White wines are usually made from white grapes, as in Chablis or a Riesling. Yet black grapes can also give a white wine. The trick is to separate the skins from the juice before fermentation, for example by pressing gently: since the colour lives in the skins, the juice stays pale and the finished wine is white.":"Los vinos blancos suelen elaborarse con uvas blancas, como un Chablis o un Riesling. Sin embargo, también se puede hacer vino blanco con uvas tintas. Basta con separar los hollejos del jugo antes de la fermentación, por ejemplo con un prensado suave: como el color está en la piel, el jugo sigue claro y el vino resulta blanco.","A red wine, on the other hand, must come from black grapes. During fermentation the skins stay in the juice and are mixed in thoroughly, so they pass colour and tannin into the wine. Once fermentation is over, the new wine is drained off the skins. Rioja from Spain and Cabernet Sauvignon wines are red examples.":"Un vino tinto, en cambio, tiene que hacerse con uvas tintas. Durante la fermentación los hollejos permanecen en el jugo y se mezclan bien con él, de modo que le ceden color y tanino. Cuando termina la fermentación, el vino se separa de los hollejos. El Rioja español y los vinos de Cabernet Sauvignon son ejemplos de tintos.","Rosé is also made from black grapes, but the skin contact is short: just a few hours. The juice, by then only pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins, giving a lightly coloured wine. White Zinfandel from California is a rosé example. Rosé wines are also only rarely aged in oak.":"El rosado también procede de uvas tintas, pero el contacto con los hollejos es breve: apenas unas horas. Después el jugo, solo ligeramente rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. El resultado es un vino de color suave. El White Zinfandel de California es un ejemplo de rosado. Además, los rosados rara vez se crían en roble.","Black grape colour is in the skin; the juice is colourless":"El color de la uva tinta está en el hollejo; el jugo es incoloro","Sweetness comes from sugar left in the wine. Most wines are dry: to make one, the yeast must turn all the sugar in the juice into alcohol, leaving little or none behind. Dry examples include Chablis and Sauvignon Blanc wines among whites, and Côtes du Rhône, Chianti and Cabernet Sauvignon wines among reds.":"El dulzor depende del azúcar que queda en el vino. La mayoría de los vinos son secos: para lograrlo, las levaduras tienen que convertir en alcohol todo el azúcar del jugo, de modo que queda muy poco o nada. Son secos, por ejemplo, el Chablis y los Sauvignon Blanc entre los blancos, y el Côtes du Rhône, el Chianti y los Cabernet Sauvignon entre los tintos.","Medium-sweet wines are mostly white or rosé. There are two main ways to make them: remove the yeast before it has turned all the sugar into alcohol, or blend some unfermented grape juice into a dry wine. Some German Rieslings and White Zinfandel, the Californian rosé, are good examples.":"Los vinos de dulzor medio son sobre todo blancos o rosados. Se elaboran de dos maneras: retirando las levaduras antes de que hayan transformado todo el azúcar, o añadiendo jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Algunos Riesling alemanes y el White Zinfandel, el rosado californiano, son buenos ejemplos.","Acidity comes straight from the grape juice, and it is what makes a wine refreshing. It is easy to spot because it makes your mouth water. Too much tastes unpleasantly sharp; too little and the wine loses its freshness. Chablis, Chianti and wines from Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon and Pinot Noir all have high acidity.":"La acidez procede directamente del jugo de uva y es lo que hace que un vino resulte refrescante. Es fácil de reconocer porque hace salivar. Demasiada acidez hace que el vino sea desagradablemente ácido; demasiado poca y pierde su frescura. El Chablis, el Chianti y los vinos de Sauvignon Blanc, Riesling, Cabernet Sauvignon y Pinot Noir tienen acidez alta.","Medium: yeast removed early, or unfermented juice added":"Medio: levaduras retiradas antes, o jugo sin fermentar añadido","Acidity: from the juice, makes the mouth water, balances sweetness":"Acidez: viene del jugo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor","Nearly all still and sparkling wines sit between 11.5% and 14% abv. A few reach 15%, while others go as low as 8%. Châteauneuf-du-Pape, a French red, is an example of a high-alcohol wine; White Zinfandel from California is an example of a low-alcohol one. Remember that alcohol is produced when yeast ferment sugar.":"Casi todos los vinos tranquilos y espumosos tienen entre un 11,5 % y un 14 % vol. Algunos llegan al 15 % y otros bajan hasta el 8 %. El Châteauneuf-du-Pape, tinto francés, es un ejemplo de vino con mucho alcohol; el White Zinfandel californiano, de vino con poco. Recordá que el alcohol se forma cuando las levaduras fermentan el azúcar.","Wine can be fermented and/or matured in oak barrels. When it is, the wood adds notes such as vanilla, coconut, cloves, cedar and smoke. The use of oak is sometimes mentioned on the label. If you pick up these aromas alongside the fruit, it is a good clue that the wine has spent time in barrel.":"El vino puede fermentar y/o criarse en barricas de roble. En ese caso la madera aporta notas de vainilla, coco, clavo, cedro y ahumado. A veces el uso de roble aparece en la etiqueta. Si notas estos aromas junto a la fruta, es una buena pista de que el vino pasó por barrica.","The skins stay in the juice during fermentation":"Los hollejos se quedan en el jugo durante la fermentación","Unfermented black grape juice is added":"Se añade jugo de uva tinta sin fermentar","The pulp of white and black grapes is the same colour and the juice is colourless. To make a red wine, black grapes are used and the skins are kept in contact with the juice throughout fermentation, mixed in well, so colour and tannin pass into the wine.":"La pulpa de las uvas blancas y tintas tiene el mismo color y el jugo es incoloro. Para hacer un tinto se usan uvas tintas y se dejan los hollejos en contacto con el jugo durante toda la fermentación, mezclándolos bien: así pasan al vino el color y el tanino.","Yes, by separating skins and juice before fermentation":"Sí, separando hollejos y jugo antes de fermentar","Black grape juice is colourless, so without the skins the wine stays white.":"El jugo de la uva tinta es incoloro: sin hollejos, el vino queda blanco.","All the colour of a black grape is in its skin. If the grapes are pressed gently and the skins are separated from the juice before fermentation, the juice stays pale and makes a white wine. This same idea is what allows Pinot Noir to be used in Champagne.":"Todo el color de la uva tinta está en su piel. Si las uvas se prensan con suavidad y los hollejos se separan del jugo antes de la fermentación, el jugo sigue claro y da un vino blanco. Es la misma idea que permite usar Pinot Noir en el Champagne.","The juice sits with black grape skins for a few hours, then is drained off.":"El jugo pasa unas horas con los hollejos de uva tinta y luego se separa.","Rosé comes from black grapes, like red wine, but the skin contact lasts only a few hours. The juice, now just pink, is drained off and finishes fermenting without the skins. If the skins stayed in until the end, the result would be a red wine instead.":"El rosado procede de uvas tintas, como el tinto, pero el contacto con los hollejos dura solo unas horas. El jugo, apenas rosado, se separa y termina de fermentar sin pieles. Si los hollejos se quedaran hasta el final, se obtendría un vino tinto.","Unfermented grape juice is added to the wine":"Se añade jugo de uva sin fermentar","Most wines are dry: the yeast keep working until they have turned all the sugar into alcohol. The other answers describe ways of keeping sugar in the wine: removing yeast or adding juice for medium wines, and adding alcohol for sweet fortified wines.":"La mayoría de los vinos son secos: las levaduras trabajan hasta convertir todo el azúcar en alcohol. Las demás respuestas describen formas de conservar azúcar: retirar las levaduras o añadir jugo en los vinos de dulzor medio, y añadir alcohol en los fortificados dulces.","Adding unfermented grape juice to a dry wine":"Añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco","Leaving the skins in the juice for longer":"Dejar los hollejos más tiempo en el jugo","Unfermented juice brings sugar back into an already dry wine.":"El jugo sin fermentar aporta azúcar a un vino ya seco.","There are two routes to a medium-sweet wine: remove the yeast before they have eaten all the sugar, or add unfermented grape juice to a dry wine. Skins and oak affect colour, tannin and aromas, not the level of sweetness.":"Hay dos caminos para un vino de dulzor medio: retirar las levaduras antes de que consuman todo el azúcar, o añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar a un vino seco. Los hollejos y el roble influyen en el color, el tanino y los aromas, no en el dulzor.","Adding unfermented grape juice to the wine":"Añadir jugo de uva sin fermentar","It adds tannin and therefore more body":"Agregá tanino y, por tanto, más cuerpo","Acidity comes from the grape juice and refreshes the wine. In sweet wines it acts as a counterweight to the sugar, which is why Sauternes and sweet Rieslings have high acidity. It does not change the colour, the tannin or the alcohol level. Without it, the wine would feel heavy.":"La acidez procede del jugo de uva y refresca el vino. En los dulces hace de contrapeso al azúcar: por eso el Sauternes y los Riesling dulces tienen acidez alta. No influye en el color, el tanino ni la graduación. Sin ella, el vino resultaría pesado.","The sugar in the juice":"El azúcar del jugo","Black grapes have coloured skins that contain tannins. When red wine ferments, the skins stay in the juice and release colour and tannin. How much tannin the wine ends up with depends on the grape and the winemaking: red Bordeaux has a lot, Beaujolais very little.":"Las uvas tintas tienen hollejos coloreados que contienen taninos. Al fermentar un tinto, los hollejos permanecen en el jugo y le ceden color y tanino. La cantidad final depende de la variedad y de la elaboración: el Bordeaux tinto tiene mucho; el Beaujolais, poco.","Beaujolais is a classic example of a low-tannin red, along with some Pinot Noir wines. Red Bordeaux and Chianti, by contrast, are standard examples of high-tannin reds, and Port, a sweet red fortified wine, also has high tannins. Remember that tannin leaves the mouth feeling dry.":"El Beaujolais es un ejemplo clásico de tinto con poco tanino, como algunos Pinot Noir. El Bordeaux tinto y el Chianti, en cambio, son ejemplos típicos de tintos muy tánicos, y el Port, vino fortificado tinto y dulce, también tiene taninos altos. Recordá que el tanino deja la boca seca.","Comes from the juice, makes the mouth water, refreshes and balances sweetness.":"Viene del jugo, hace salivar, refresca y equilibra el dulzor."}};
